WEBVTT

00:15.724 --> 00:17.934
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:23.106 --> 00:26.025
FINAL EPISODE

00:26.526 --> 00:28.319
We ordered the beer ages ago.

00:29.070 --> 00:30.947
Why is it taking so long?

00:34.492 --> 00:37.996
PUB BY THE HOSPITAL

00:38.079 --> 00:40.623
I bought these for you guys.

00:41.332 --> 00:42.625
Looks refreshing, right?

00:42.709 --> 00:44.627
Why are you acting out of character?

00:44.711 --> 00:45.545
I guess we're right.

00:45.628 --> 00:48.047
All right. Let's drink these
and start talking.

00:48.131 --> 00:50.341
Cheers. Bottoms up.

00:55.764 --> 00:56.890
So?

00:56.973 --> 00:57.849
For real?

00:57.932 --> 00:59.017
You two are…

00:59.934 --> 01:01.269
You see…

01:05.648 --> 01:07.108
Here are your beers.

01:08.401 --> 01:09.986
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

01:11.488 --> 01:12.697
That was great timing.

01:21.581 --> 01:23.625
I live with
my sister's brother-in-law, Dr. Ku.

01:27.670 --> 01:28.963
We're dating. Happy now?

01:29.839 --> 01:31.049
-Holy cow!
-It really is true.

01:31.132 --> 01:32.634
-You were right.
-Hey, can you stop--

01:32.717 --> 01:34.344
See? I told you I saw them!

01:34.427 --> 01:36.387
Hey, Yi-young. I kept it a secret though.

01:36.471 --> 01:38.097
Hey, when did you start dating?

01:38.181 --> 01:39.098
Who liked who first?

01:39.182 --> 01:40.058
Does your family know?

01:40.141 --> 01:42.310
Wait, that's double in-laws.
You'll be double in-laws?

01:42.393 --> 01:45.063
Look, I'll handle my own relationship,

01:45.146 --> 01:46.856
so stop worrying about it.

01:47.565 --> 01:50.109
Just keep it a secret at work for me.

01:50.193 --> 01:51.319
Okay.

01:51.402 --> 01:54.155
It would only be a headache
if people at work knew.

01:55.198 --> 01:56.366
I don't have anyone to tell.

01:56.449 --> 01:57.408
But, Yi-young.

01:58.159 --> 01:59.744
We feel hurt.

01:59.828 --> 02:01.538
You should've told us.

02:01.621 --> 02:02.914
That's…

02:06.209 --> 02:07.085
I'm sorry.

02:08.586 --> 02:10.380
All right. We'll forgive you.

02:11.005 --> 02:13.258
So with that in mind, this one's on you.

02:17.053 --> 02:18.596
Let's get dried pollack. It's good.

02:18.680 --> 02:20.056
The whelks and cuttlefish too.

02:20.140 --> 02:22.058
We ordered some squid earlier.

02:22.142 --> 02:23.101
-Excuse me!
-Order more.

02:23.184 --> 02:24.811
Dried pollack, whelks, and cuttlefish.

02:24.894 --> 02:26.062
-Nachos too.
-French fries.

02:26.146 --> 02:28.273
-And nachos and fries, please.
-Don't order those yet!

02:38.241 --> 02:40.869
Doctor, about Ms. Lee Sang-lim in MFICU…

02:40.952 --> 02:42.871
I prescribed her a uterine relaxant,

02:42.954 --> 02:44.330
so you can hook it up for her.

02:44.414 --> 02:46.166
And for Ms. Kim Go-yun,

02:46.249 --> 02:49.544
I checked her personal medication,
and she can take them all.

02:51.129 --> 02:53.006
Your hands are moving like a blur.

02:54.382 --> 02:55.300
I know, right?

02:55.383 --> 02:59.095
I can't believe this used to be so hard
I had to stay after work to do it.

03:01.723 --> 03:02.891
Are you going somewhere?

03:04.017 --> 03:05.518
I have a date tonight.

03:06.185 --> 03:08.605
You're so lucky. Gosh, I'm jealous.

03:08.688 --> 03:10.398
Are you on a break from dating these days?

03:10.481 --> 03:12.442
Not a break. I'm out of business.

03:12.525 --> 03:15.403
I mean, I'm always at the hospital,
so how can I meet people?

03:16.654 --> 03:18.573
I guess that's why
people date their coworkers.

03:18.656 --> 03:19.782
Date their coworkers?

03:21.826 --> 03:23.161
Someone's dating their coworker?

03:23.244 --> 03:24.078
What?

03:28.625 --> 03:30.752
I'm not sure if I should say this.

03:30.835 --> 03:33.171
Besides Dr. Oh's relationship,
there's another couple?

03:33.880 --> 03:34.881
Wait, how did you know?

03:37.592 --> 03:38.760
Well…

03:41.387 --> 03:43.806
Nurse, I said it was a secret!

03:50.688 --> 03:52.815
-And…
-There's more?

03:52.899 --> 03:56.110
I requested a GS consult for Ms. Yun
and scheduled her operation.

03:57.237 --> 03:58.321
How did you know that?

03:58.404 --> 04:00.782
Did… I ask you to do it?

04:01.407 --> 04:04.869
Her chart said she had wanted
a chemo port even before surgery,

04:04.953 --> 04:06.454
so I only got it ready.

04:10.583 --> 04:13.002
And Ms. Na Seo-hyeon
was scheduled for a BSO,

04:13.086 --> 04:15.922
but she wanted ovary preservation,
so I changed it to a BOC.

04:16.005 --> 04:17.423
Just in case you forgot.

04:18.132 --> 04:19.300
Nice work.

04:19.384 --> 04:20.927
-Thank you.
-Hello, sir.

04:21.010 --> 04:22.053
Hi, Dr. Ku.

04:22.136 --> 04:23.096
The study group.

04:24.597 --> 04:25.723
You didn't join?

04:26.224 --> 04:29.894
I see. So there's nothing more
for you to learn?

04:29.978 --> 04:31.271
No, there's a ton to learn.

04:31.354 --> 04:34.274
But I'm so busy right now,
so I was planning to join in January.

04:34.857 --> 04:36.150
We lost him to OB.

04:36.234 --> 04:38.569
This diligent and talented doctor.

04:39.237 --> 04:40.071
Thank you, sir.

04:41.072 --> 04:42.740
I should get going.

04:42.824 --> 04:44.325
-Goodbye.
-Bye.

04:47.120 --> 04:48.496
For a variety of reasons,

04:48.579 --> 04:49.664
it's such a shame.

04:49.747 --> 04:50.790
If I had a daughter…

04:50.873 --> 04:52.375
Even if you did, it wouldn't matter.

04:55.295 --> 04:56.713
He has a girlfriend.

04:58.089 --> 04:58.923
Really?

05:00.258 --> 05:01.968
What? Who?

05:03.803 --> 05:05.096
It's a secret.

05:09.058 --> 05:10.059
Someone from work, right?

05:10.143 --> 05:11.644
Yes, it's Oh Yi-young.

05:11.728 --> 05:13.771
Right, Oh Yi-young. The…

05:13.855 --> 05:15.398
The one with the short hair?

05:15.481 --> 05:16.399
No, long hair.

05:16.482 --> 05:18.526
Right, and she's tall?

05:18.609 --> 05:20.611
No, she's shorter than me.

05:20.695 --> 05:21.529
Really?

05:23.239 --> 05:25.658
I know. It must be her.

05:25.742 --> 05:27.744
The intern planning to go to Neurology.

05:29.996 --> 05:30.997
Yes, that's right.

05:32.206 --> 05:34.167
Those two?

05:34.876 --> 05:36.961
They're very…

05:37.045 --> 05:38.004
Since when?

05:38.546 --> 05:39.547
Has it been long?

05:41.049 --> 05:43.134
The surgery schedule
will be hectic tomorrow.

05:43.843 --> 05:45.136
I looked into it.

05:45.970 --> 05:47.764
OR 7 will likely be free first.

05:47.847 --> 05:49.974
So how about putting
the TLH as OR 7's last surgery

05:50.058 --> 05:51.851
and having the explo-laparotomy in OR 10?

05:53.227 --> 05:54.228
That would work.

05:54.812 --> 05:55.897
You figured that out quick.

05:57.899 --> 05:59.650
I never thought
I'd live long enough to see

05:59.734 --> 06:01.027
such an incredible sight.

06:02.528 --> 06:04.030
This is nothing, Doctor.

06:06.824 --> 06:09.827
There's something else
that really is incredible though.

06:16.292 --> 06:17.460
About Dr. Ku…

06:18.878 --> 06:20.129
They're still together?

06:20.797 --> 06:21.714
What?

06:21.798 --> 06:24.717
I thought he and Dr. Oh would break up,
but they're lasting a long time.

06:24.801 --> 06:26.719
Wait, how did you know?

06:26.803 --> 06:29.222
What do you mean? It was pretty obvious.

06:30.264 --> 06:32.433
I have to go. See you later.

06:33.142 --> 06:35.478
A secret relationship, my foot.
It's only secret to them.

06:36.145 --> 06:38.022
Everyone at work knows. Everyone.

06:38.106 --> 06:38.981
Do you know too?

06:40.566 --> 06:43.319
Your savings matured as of December 29th.

06:43.402 --> 06:45.863
The amount listed there
will be deposited now.

06:45.947 --> 06:47.907
Not many people make it to five years.

06:47.990 --> 06:48.866
It's very impressive.

06:49.450 --> 06:50.326
Thank you.

06:57.083 --> 06:59.502
Would you like to hear
about any other products?

07:00.086 --> 07:02.421
I'd like to open
another one-year savings account.

07:02.505 --> 07:04.257
So you need short-term savings plan?

07:04.340 --> 07:05.174
Yes.

07:06.467 --> 07:08.136
I think I'll need the money soon.

07:09.762 --> 07:11.347
By soon…

07:11.430 --> 07:12.473
Do you mean…

07:12.557 --> 07:13.558
For a wedding fund?

07:14.142 --> 07:14.976
Yes.

07:23.901 --> 07:26.237
What on earth?
Why are you here making a ruckus?

07:26.320 --> 07:28.448
Are you prepped for rounds?
What about the charts?

07:31.409 --> 07:33.035
Go away. Now.

07:33.119 --> 07:35.079
Yes, sir. Then,

07:35.663 --> 07:38.416
your sisters-in-law
and brother-in-law will leave you to it.

07:41.711 --> 07:42.587
It's Yi-young!

07:47.425 --> 07:50.761
-Go! Now! Go do your work!
-Bye!

07:53.097 --> 07:54.348
What a bunch of kids.

08:02.773 --> 08:05.985
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

08:06.569 --> 08:08.946
Have you decided
on who the new OB professor will be?

08:09.030 --> 08:11.782
We've narrowed it down to two
based on your feedback.

08:11.866 --> 08:14.243
But our OB chief, Prof. Seo,

08:14.327 --> 08:16.204
would like a bit more time.

08:17.497 --> 08:20.124
Both candidates
have great evaluations in teaching

08:20.208 --> 08:21.959
and extensive work
and research experience.

08:22.043 --> 08:24.879
But they were a bit lacking
in other evaluation criteria.

08:24.962 --> 08:27.924
I'd like to review those areas
a bit more before deciding.

08:28.007 --> 08:31.093
Then why don't we decide
on appointing a professor next week?

08:31.177 --> 08:32.803
Yes, that sounds good.

08:32.887 --> 08:33.846
Thank you, everyone!

08:34.555 --> 08:35.848
Thank you.

08:39.477 --> 08:40.853
-Rounds?
-Yeah.

08:47.610 --> 08:50.446
2024 NON-TENURE FACULTY APPLICATION
MYEONG EUN-WON

08:51.948 --> 08:53.574
Time sure does fly.

08:54.242 --> 08:56.202
There's only one day left in this year.

08:57.119 --> 08:59.121
It feels like
we did introductions just yesterday.

08:59.205 --> 09:00.039
I know.

09:01.207 --> 09:03.125
But we're already 29.

09:04.001 --> 09:05.461
I can't believe it.

09:06.420 --> 09:09.924
Right? Seeing as how you still
throw money away like a child.

09:13.761 --> 09:16.013
It's a Christmas gift to myself.

09:17.014 --> 09:18.683
You gifted yourself last month too.

09:19.183 --> 09:20.017
The necklace.

09:22.061 --> 09:24.313
It was 68% off for Black Friday.

09:24.397 --> 09:25.273
How could I not?

09:25.356 --> 09:26.190
I had to buy it.

09:26.774 --> 09:30.319
Once she drowns in debt after maxing out
an overdraft account, then she'll wake up.

09:30.403 --> 09:31.946
Geez, enough with the nagging.

09:32.029 --> 09:33.614
You're worse than my mom.

09:36.993 --> 09:38.077
He's so loud.

09:38.160 --> 09:39.495
He didn't go home again?

09:39.579 --> 09:42.373
No, he's been pulling
all-nighters in the ward for days.

09:42.456 --> 09:43.457
Why?

09:43.541 --> 09:45.668
There's a cervical cancer patient in GYN,

09:45.751 --> 09:47.795
and it seems her cancer pain is severe.

09:47.878 --> 09:50.715
Painkillers must not be working,
because she calls every two hours.

09:50.798 --> 09:52.633
Can't he wait in here
until he gets called?

09:52.717 --> 09:54.885
He says he feels better being nearby.

09:54.969 --> 09:56.971
And he feels bad she's alone.

09:58.264 --> 09:59.265
She wasn't alone though.

09:59.348 --> 10:00.933
She has a full-time caregiver.

10:01.517 --> 10:04.020
No, that's not what we meant
by "being alone."

10:04.103 --> 10:04.937
Her family…

10:06.063 --> 10:07.231
Do I have to explain this?

10:09.025 --> 10:10.693
One is too warm,

10:11.569 --> 10:12.903
and the other is too cold.

10:13.946 --> 10:16.282
It'd be nice if we could mix you two up.

10:16.866 --> 10:19.493
But you're like oil and water.

10:28.294 --> 10:29.170
Yes?

10:30.796 --> 10:31.839
Yes, I'm on my way.

10:40.222 --> 10:41.432
Hello.

10:42.475 --> 10:44.894
So, were you able to get some sleep?

10:46.312 --> 10:49.023
I couldn't sleep again at all, Doctor.

10:50.816 --> 10:53.944
My back and hips

10:55.946 --> 10:58.824
feel like they're being ripped apart.

11:00.326 --> 11:01.827
Have you been controlling the pain?

11:01.911 --> 11:04.455
Yes, morphine is
being administered intravenously.

11:05.414 --> 11:08.501
She complained of pain overnight,
so we increased dosing frequency.

11:11.879 --> 11:15.508
But lying in bed for too long
can cause clots.

11:15.591 --> 11:17.718
So it may be hard, but moving around--

11:17.802 --> 11:19.887
How can I?

11:21.430 --> 11:24.225
I'm in too much pain.

11:26.394 --> 11:27.228
Of course.

11:28.437 --> 11:29.397
I'm sorry.

11:32.608 --> 11:34.026
Check in on her frequently.

11:34.110 --> 11:34.944
Yes, sir.

11:39.990 --> 11:43.327
Ma'am, I'll be at the station
at all times.

11:43.411 --> 11:46.038
Call me anytime if the pain's too much.
I'll come right over.

11:54.213 --> 11:55.881
You look so tired.

11:56.507 --> 11:57.425
Are you okay?

11:58.592 --> 11:59.552
I'm fine.

12:01.345 --> 12:02.930
There's not much I can do,

12:03.431 --> 12:05.224
but I should still check on her.

12:05.307 --> 12:07.643
This is why all the patients ask for you.

12:08.185 --> 12:11.147
Nurse, being asked for is a good thing.

12:11.772 --> 12:13.274
It means you're useful.

12:14.066 --> 12:15.359
Just a few months ago,

12:15.443 --> 12:17.111
no one even noticed when I was gone.

12:17.194 --> 12:18.237
I was invisible.

12:19.572 --> 12:20.739
-Really?
-Yes.

12:21.240 --> 12:24.535
After it happened to me, I realized
nothing's sadder than being useless.

12:27.621 --> 12:28.789
Did something happen?

12:31.292 --> 12:33.169
-Hello.
-Hello.

12:52.521 --> 12:53.355
What happened?

12:54.023 --> 12:58.486
The first patient Dr. Ki took on
when she arrived at Jongno Yulje…

13:00.821 --> 13:01.906
passed away.

13:04.366 --> 13:06.243
Eun-mi was in charge
from her first admission

13:06.327 --> 13:07.953
to her last cancer treatment.

13:08.954 --> 13:11.540
But she suddenly passed,
so it's hitting her harder.

13:12.124 --> 13:14.793
She has time before surgery,
so let her cry it out.

13:14.877 --> 13:16.837
-Call me for anything urgent.
-Yes, sir.

13:27.806 --> 13:28.974
It's not time for rounds.

13:33.062 --> 13:34.104
Goodness.

13:34.188 --> 13:37.024
Ms. So Won-ju.

13:37.816 --> 13:39.568
Is it because your surgery's approaching?

13:40.778 --> 13:42.112
You seem pretty worried.

13:44.281 --> 13:46.450
I thought I'd be fine the second time,

13:47.034 --> 13:47.993
but I'm not.

13:49.203 --> 13:50.871
I'm so scared I can't sleep.

13:52.373 --> 13:54.250
But you need to sleep well
before the big day.

13:54.333 --> 13:55.751
By the way, Professor.

13:56.627 --> 13:58.546
You're here alone again today.

13:58.629 --> 13:59.463
Yes, I am.

14:00.464 --> 14:02.800
I am Solo is trending these days.

14:03.467 --> 14:05.844
How about I give you a Super Surgery Pass…

14:07.429 --> 14:09.807
I mean, famous doctors at other hospitals

14:09.890 --> 14:11.892
would always have
a group of juniors in tow.

14:13.477 --> 14:16.188
And they say you can't see doctors much
because they're so busy.

14:16.272 --> 14:18.440
But you come by very often.

14:19.858 --> 14:23.070
I mean, we came for a renowned surgeon,
so I'm just making sure.

14:23.153 --> 14:26.782
First of all, I'm not a renowned doctor.

14:27.366 --> 14:31.537
I just work hard
on surgeries and treatments.

14:31.620 --> 14:33.497
That's about all I do.

14:34.415 --> 14:35.749
I like to make rounds.

14:35.833 --> 14:38.669
But having my juniors in tow
every time I do that

14:38.752 --> 14:41.547
would be an inconvenience.

14:42.423 --> 14:43.632
And it's a waste of manpower.

14:44.425 --> 14:47.011
Also, that kind of stuff
only happens on TV.

14:47.595 --> 14:48.512
But in real life,

14:49.179 --> 14:52.224
no one goes around
with a big group like that.

14:54.018 --> 14:57.271
Well, they say you do
the most surgeries here at this hospital.

14:57.354 --> 14:58.772
That much is true, right?

14:58.856 --> 14:59.815
Yes, that's right.

15:01.525 --> 15:03.694
He does a lot of surgeries, and he's good.

15:03.777 --> 15:05.237
You don't have to worry.

15:05.946 --> 15:08.908
And he appeared on a TV show
that features only renowned doctors.

15:08.991 --> 15:11.327
They call him the superstar of Yulje.

15:11.911 --> 15:13.245
Is that so?

15:13.329 --> 15:15.873
Wait, hold on. Don't get so excited.

15:15.956 --> 15:17.374
What are you doing?

15:17.458 --> 15:19.668
What's with you? Why are you saying that?

15:19.752 --> 15:20.586
Stop.

15:20.669 --> 15:22.630
-I'm done, sir.
-You are?

15:22.713 --> 15:24.298
I see. What brings you here?

15:24.381 --> 15:25.841
The patient's results are in.

15:26.383 --> 15:28.385
Hemoglobin was in the nines
at outpatient care.

15:28.469 --> 15:30.346
But the pre-op lab shows it's in the 12s.

15:31.263 --> 15:32.264
That's good news.

15:33.307 --> 15:35.392
Because of pelvic adhesions,

15:35.476 --> 15:37.937
bleeding is the main concern
for this surgery.

15:38.562 --> 15:40.147
But with numbers like these,

15:40.773 --> 15:42.483
we won't need a preemptive transfusion.

15:42.566 --> 15:43.734
That's fantastic.

15:44.318 --> 15:45.402
That's a relief.

15:45.486 --> 15:47.363
After hearing only bad news all the time,

15:48.072 --> 15:49.782
hearing some good news

15:49.865 --> 15:51.742
does make me feel a bit better.

15:53.202 --> 15:54.954
We got a positive sign,

15:55.037 --> 15:57.289
so you can sleep well tonight.

15:58.040 --> 16:01.293
We'll do our best tomorrow during surgery.

16:01.377 --> 16:03.379
-Yes, thank you.
-Thank you.

16:04.880 --> 16:05.756
Thank you.

16:06.674 --> 16:08.092
I so wish that Ms. So

16:08.175 --> 16:10.844
will sleep soundly tonight.

16:18.310 --> 16:19.979
I got verbal confirmation from Radiology

16:20.062 --> 16:22.314
and contacted
a Vascular Surgery professor via consult.

16:23.065 --> 16:23.899
Already?

16:23.983 --> 16:25.526
I ordered more blood for transfusions,

16:25.609 --> 16:27.361
re-briefed Anesthesiology
about the patient,

16:27.444 --> 16:29.279
and rechecked the bed
in the ICU this morning.

16:29.363 --> 16:30.197
So,

16:31.115 --> 16:33.450
it's okay take a breath.

16:33.534 --> 16:34.368
Yes, sir.

16:35.869 --> 16:36.829
What is it?

16:37.788 --> 16:38.706
Are you worried?

16:39.456 --> 16:40.332
Yes.

16:40.958 --> 16:44.461
There are severe adhesions
from the pelvic wall to the bowels,

16:44.545 --> 16:46.797
so I think there will be heavy bleeding.

16:46.880 --> 16:48.298
Yes, there will be.

16:48.382 --> 16:51.051
You've done it many times,
so I'm sure you're okay,

16:51.135 --> 16:52.344
but for me,

16:53.095 --> 16:56.306
I still get scared
when there's heavy bleeding.

16:56.390 --> 16:57.599
I feel the same way.

16:58.934 --> 17:00.394
I also get very scared.

17:01.812 --> 17:02.896
I get terrified.

17:03.814 --> 17:07.735
It's like this. The patient didn't give up
on surgery and got her labs up.

17:07.818 --> 17:10.320
She's done her part.

17:10.404 --> 17:11.530
So now,

17:11.613 --> 17:13.782
the rest is up to us.

17:14.366 --> 17:16.410
And on top of that,
if there's heavy bleeding,

17:16.493 --> 17:17.494
it's really scary.

17:18.203 --> 17:19.121
I lose sleep too.

17:20.080 --> 17:22.374
That's why I keep doing rounds,

17:23.417 --> 17:24.626
try to make jokes,

17:25.252 --> 17:26.962
and assure them things will be okay.

17:27.838 --> 17:28.964
That's what I'm doing.

17:30.966 --> 17:32.760
So, I wanted to ask…

17:34.053 --> 17:35.304
For some encouragement,

17:36.263 --> 17:37.306
can you repeat…

17:39.558 --> 17:40.893
what you said earlier?

17:41.518 --> 17:42.352
Sorry?

17:42.436 --> 17:45.147
You know. What you said to the patient…

17:46.065 --> 17:49.026
That you do the most surgeries
and are the best at them?

17:49.109 --> 17:50.652
Not that. That's not important.

17:50.736 --> 17:51.945
You were on Best Doctors?

17:55.699 --> 17:57.493
The superstar of Yulje?

18:02.623 --> 18:03.749
"Superstar."

18:04.917 --> 18:06.251
But still,

18:06.335 --> 18:09.630
how can I call myself a superstar
like I'm Lim Young-woong or something?

18:10.297 --> 18:11.381
That's a bit…

18:12.591 --> 18:15.511
You might offend some people.
They'll storm the hospital.

18:20.599 --> 18:21.642
-Then too?
-Yes.

18:21.725 --> 18:22.601
Professor?

18:23.519 --> 18:26.271
The patients I updated you about
have entered the labor room.

18:27.064 --> 18:28.190
Okay, let's go.

18:28.899 --> 18:30.275
-Thank you.
-Of course.

18:36.657 --> 18:37.616
Hello, ma'am.

18:37.699 --> 18:38.534
Hello.

18:39.118 --> 18:42.037
Nam Seol-i at 39 weeks and 5 days.
Multigravida, last birth in 2015.

18:42.788 --> 18:44.039
Cervix is fingertip-soft,

18:44.123 --> 18:46.750
but contractions were every ten minutes,
so we admitted her.

18:47.417 --> 18:50.337
Labor usually progresses faster
with the second baby.

18:51.088 --> 18:54.174
But it's been eight years
since you last gave birth,

18:54.758 --> 18:58.303
and at this rate,
you won't be having the baby today.

18:59.054 --> 18:59.930
Okay.

19:00.472 --> 19:02.432
Maybe it's because I've done it once.

19:03.058 --> 19:04.560
But I feel more scared, Professor.

19:04.643 --> 19:07.062
Things will go much smoother. Don't worry.

19:07.146 --> 19:09.148
-Oh, my. It's that good?
-By the way…

19:09.231 --> 19:11.859
You said the baby
was on the larger side last time…

19:12.776 --> 19:13.777
No way!

19:14.987 --> 19:17.906
But I could give birth on the 31st.

19:20.701 --> 19:21.869
So you're saying

19:21.952 --> 19:25.455
a birth on New Year's Day
would bring the most fortune, right?

19:26.999 --> 19:28.834
Even better if it's born at midnight?

19:30.460 --> 19:33.881
But I can't believe how a single day
makes such a difference in luck.

19:33.964 --> 19:36.008
So the 31st is really bad, right?

19:39.803 --> 19:40.637
I'm sorry.

19:41.722 --> 19:42.556
I'll be done soon.

19:43.557 --> 19:44.725
I'm sorry.

19:46.852 --> 19:49.188
She went through a lot
to get pregnant through IVF,

19:49.271 --> 19:50.772
so she's especially eager.

19:51.607 --> 19:53.817
And tomorrow's the 31st.

19:53.901 --> 19:56.111
Among mothers
who go into labor at this period,

19:56.737 --> 19:59.656
some get greedy
and want a New Year's baby.

20:00.657 --> 20:03.160
It's giving birth
right at midnight on January 1st.

20:04.953 --> 20:06.955
So that's why they're all making a fuss?

20:08.332 --> 20:09.708
Hello!

20:10.542 --> 20:13.503
Well, the thing is
my water suddenly broke,

20:13.587 --> 20:15.422
so my due date got pushed up.

20:15.505 --> 20:17.174
But guess what?

20:17.257 --> 20:19.676
They say our little darling
could be born tomorrow.

20:20.344 --> 20:22.429
So, since I'm here now,

20:22.512 --> 20:24.598
I'll try to give birth
to a New Year's baby.

20:25.182 --> 20:27.851
I'll give birth on January 1st at midnight

20:27.935 --> 20:30.520
and share that magical energy
with you all.

20:30.604 --> 20:32.481
Subscribe, like,
and turn on notifications…

20:33.106 --> 20:34.358
Oh, my goodness.

20:34.441 --> 20:36.610
I'm so sorry.
It's for content we're creating.

20:36.693 --> 20:39.196
-I'm sorry.
-I'm sorry. Excuse me.

20:44.952 --> 20:48.163
A healthy baby is enough.
What more do you want?

20:50.916 --> 20:53.085
The doljabi isn't that important.

20:57.506 --> 20:58.715
Hey, Min-hye.

20:59.466 --> 21:02.261
I really wanted to come celebrate
your baby's first birthday,

21:03.095 --> 21:05.389
but it's my mother-in-law's
birthday that day.

21:07.683 --> 21:09.476
Don't feel bad for inviting me.

21:11.687 --> 21:13.939
I'm more upset
at how cautious you're being around me.

21:15.274 --> 21:19.152
I had another transfer this week,
and I'll do a blood test soon.

21:19.236 --> 21:21.822
It's going to be fine. Don't worry.

21:23.240 --> 21:24.283
I'm really fine.

21:27.452 --> 21:30.163
Okay, let's talk again soon. Bye.

21:32.249 --> 21:33.083
Seung-won!

21:33.166 --> 21:34.334
Yes, dear?

21:34.418 --> 21:35.836
What? Is that you, dear?

21:36.878 --> 21:38.714
It's cold out. What are you doing here?

21:43.802 --> 21:44.636
Did you hear?

21:44.720 --> 21:45.804
No.

21:45.887 --> 21:47.139
Then why did you walk away?

21:50.392 --> 21:51.226
I was cold.

21:59.443 --> 22:00.485
You know Min-hye, right?

22:00.569 --> 22:02.821
Yeah, she's your closest friend.

22:02.904 --> 22:06.033
She gave a speech at our wedding
and came to Yi-young's graduation.

22:07.075 --> 22:08.660
She had a hard time conceiving

22:08.744 --> 22:10.787
-and came to our hospital last year.
-Right.

22:10.871 --> 22:13.999
But she got pregnant
on her first try with IVF.

22:17.919 --> 22:19.254
The baby's already a year old.

22:21.048 --> 22:22.049
So cute, right?

22:22.716 --> 22:23.717
So cute.

22:27.471 --> 22:29.514
What's wrong?
You don't want to go to the party?

22:31.391 --> 22:32.225
No.

22:34.186 --> 22:35.937
I can't bring myself to congratulate her.

22:37.731 --> 22:39.149
So I lied.

22:40.192 --> 22:41.151
Good.

22:44.654 --> 22:47.532
I'm mad she invited me to the party,

22:49.659 --> 22:51.870
I'm upset
that she's so cautious around me,

22:53.246 --> 22:56.249
and I'm annoyed
that she asked me if I'm okay.

22:58.043 --> 22:59.753
But what I hate most right now is…

23:02.130 --> 23:03.507
how jealous

23:04.216 --> 23:06.551
and petty I'm being.

23:07.886 --> 23:09.971
The blood test is in a few days.

23:10.931 --> 23:12.557
You're just on edge right now.

23:16.853 --> 23:18.438
All this fuss to get pregnant.

23:21.191 --> 23:23.318
It's turning me into a mess.

23:23.401 --> 23:24.653
You're not a mess.

23:26.029 --> 23:27.030
It's understandable.

23:29.282 --> 23:30.367
I totally get it.

23:37.082 --> 23:38.750
Gosh, your hands are so cold.

23:38.834 --> 23:40.001
Let's go in, okay?

23:40.752 --> 23:42.587
It's so cold.

23:44.589 --> 23:46.424
Let's go in. It's so cold!

23:49.177 --> 23:51.930
You don't have a moving date yet.
Why are you already packing?

23:52.013 --> 23:54.474
I wanted to pack in advance
while I had the time.

23:54.558 --> 23:57.018
In your second year,
you'll be too busy to clean your room.

23:57.102 --> 23:58.478
Should I stop here and help you?

23:58.562 --> 23:59.771
I cleaned it last week.

24:02.315 --> 24:03.316
No, you didn't.

24:04.151 --> 24:05.193
I did.

24:06.236 --> 24:07.445
That's the cleaned room?

24:12.409 --> 24:14.536
Will I become too busy
to see you next year then?

24:15.203 --> 24:16.413
I'll be doing more deliveries.

24:16.997 --> 24:17.873
That's right.

24:17.956 --> 24:20.208
But you'll do less
of your first-year duties.

24:20.292 --> 24:21.835
I heard we may not get a first-year.

24:24.421 --> 24:26.089
That will make things really hard.

24:26.173 --> 24:28.258
It's okay. I can just quit.

24:28.341 --> 24:29.342
Again with that.

24:30.719 --> 24:32.095
I'm just saying I could.

24:33.513 --> 24:35.473
I stay on until I'm debt-free,
so don't worry.

24:37.475 --> 24:38.810
But I'm almost done.

24:38.894 --> 24:40.270
Now, I'm down to 19 million.

24:40.353 --> 24:41.938
You've paid off a lot.

24:45.775 --> 24:47.903
I'm never using
an overdraft account again.

24:55.368 --> 24:57.454
It's too messy in there.

24:57.537 --> 24:59.873
I'll clean it up myself next time.

25:01.291 --> 25:02.334
I see. Okay, then.

25:15.555 --> 25:16.890
"To my Do-won."

25:18.225 --> 25:20.852
"All that studying must be tough.
Right, Do-won?"

25:23.521 --> 25:24.898
"I miss you so much."

25:24.981 --> 25:27.025
-"It's so hard to bear."
-That's not mine!

25:27.108 --> 25:30.445
"Sometimes, I think I like you more
than you like me."

25:30.528 --> 25:32.280
"It makes me so sad!"

25:46.378 --> 25:47.587
What are you two doing?

25:50.882 --> 25:52.175
Are you two…

25:58.807 --> 26:00.767
Are you two physically fighting now?

26:00.850 --> 26:02.310
Yi-young, move your elbow.

26:02.394 --> 26:04.312
That's the solar plexus. You'll kill him.

26:05.897 --> 26:07.774
When is that idiot ever going to grow up?

26:08.400 --> 26:09.526
Are you sick?

26:12.237 --> 26:13.196
I'm healthy!

26:14.239 --> 26:15.532
We didn't fight!

26:16.116 --> 26:17.826
I was helping him!

26:40.598 --> 26:41.474
Oh, right.

26:50.233 --> 26:51.943
Please…

26:57.699 --> 26:59.284
Damn it.

26:59.367 --> 27:00.327
I always lose.

27:12.839 --> 27:14.799
When did I buy this?

27:24.100 --> 27:26.394
CONGRATULATIONS!
YOU'VE WON 32,984,892 WON

27:41.076 --> 27:43.953
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

27:44.871 --> 27:46.790
One hot Americano, please.

27:47.791 --> 27:49.167
That'll be 1,500 won.

27:52.670 --> 27:53.922
You're all set.

28:00.553 --> 28:02.097
Hello, this is Oh Yi-young.

28:02.180 --> 28:04.432
Hello, this is your bank.

28:04.516 --> 28:06.976
We're calling you
about extending your overdraft account.

28:07.060 --> 28:08.728
Oh, yes.

28:08.812 --> 28:10.772
If you'd like to extend it next year…

28:10.855 --> 28:13.066
I need to come
with my certificate of employment, right?

28:13.149 --> 28:15.443
Yes. If you don't have plans to extend it,

28:15.527 --> 28:18.363
you can repay
the amount of 19,750,300 won.

28:18.446 --> 28:19.489
I'll repay it.

28:20.156 --> 28:21.157
I won't be extending it.

28:21.241 --> 28:22.283
All right.

28:22.367 --> 28:25.620
In that case, the account will remain
only until January 21st.

28:25.703 --> 28:26.579
Okay.

28:27.163 --> 28:27.997
Thank you.

28:35.505 --> 28:36.339
Dr. Oh?

28:39.092 --> 28:40.260
Good morning, Doctor.

28:40.343 --> 28:42.470
You have this month's
delivery stats, right?

28:42.554 --> 28:44.139
Can you email them to me by tonight?

28:44.889 --> 28:47.726
Patient and baby data from today
needs to be included as well.

28:49.686 --> 28:51.354
I'll need more time then--

28:51.438 --> 28:53.606
And I need to do ultrasounds
for MFICU patients.

28:53.690 --> 28:55.400
Go and have them prepped for me now.

28:59.654 --> 29:01.072
Drink your coffee first though.

29:04.117 --> 29:05.243
It's okay.

29:05.326 --> 29:07.036
I'll get right on it.

29:07.704 --> 29:10.165
If you're getting coffee,
you can take my place in line.

29:13.168 --> 29:14.002
What on earth?

29:15.754 --> 29:16.838
Why is she being so scary?

29:28.141 --> 29:29.809
I've never seen this before.

29:33.730 --> 29:35.732
Hey! It's morning. Get up.

29:38.443 --> 29:39.319
Already?

29:40.361 --> 29:41.780
Did you stay up in the ward again?

29:41.863 --> 29:42.697
Yeah.

29:44.032 --> 29:46.868
Ms. Hong Sa-ra's pain is getting worse.

29:51.372 --> 29:52.373
She keeps calling.

29:56.419 --> 29:58.880
But is it okay
to give her drugs that often?

29:58.963 --> 29:59.881
Isn't it too much?

29:59.964 --> 30:01.549
I don't go to give her drugs.

30:01.633 --> 30:03.384
I just check to see if she's okay.

30:04.260 --> 30:05.678
I see. You check.

30:07.514 --> 30:08.431
What do you check?

30:09.682 --> 30:13.186
The worse her pain gets,
the more depressed and lonely she becomes.

30:13.770 --> 30:15.730
I keep her company and chat with her.

30:19.108 --> 30:19.943
But

30:21.528 --> 30:23.530
does that make her pain hurt less?

30:25.156 --> 30:28.034
I mean, she didn't ask you
to come keep her company.

30:28.117 --> 30:29.536
She called because she's in pain.

30:32.413 --> 30:33.414
You're so cold.

30:34.040 --> 30:36.501
You said it's an advanced cancer mass
with severe pelvic pain

30:36.584 --> 30:38.294
and her whole body aches from metastasis.

30:38.878 --> 30:41.714
She's had three days of IV morphine,
but the pain hasn't subsided.

30:41.798 --> 30:42.632
Yeah.

30:43.424 --> 30:45.385
That's why I'm so worried I can't go home.

30:46.761 --> 30:48.012
That's not what I mean.

30:51.891 --> 30:54.894
I guess we really are like water and oil.

30:57.605 --> 30:59.899
Hey. Where are you going?

30:59.983 --> 31:00.817
Surgery!

31:21.212 --> 31:25.800
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER
SURGERY STATUS

31:25.884 --> 31:28.386
GOODBYE 2023
SENDING OFF THE LAST SUNSET WITH HOPE

31:28.469 --> 31:35.435
ANESTHESIA TIME, CURRENT TIME,
SURGERY TIME

31:39.188 --> 31:40.106
How are her vitals?

31:40.189 --> 31:41.107
Her BP's low.

31:42.233 --> 31:43.318
EBL's 1,100.

31:43.985 --> 31:46.112
I'm using vasopressors while transfusing,

31:46.195 --> 31:47.822
but her vitals aren't stable, Professor.

31:47.906 --> 31:50.700
We fully removed the tumor
and stopped most of the bleeding,

31:51.326 --> 31:52.869
but the entire pelvic floor is oozing.

31:54.495 --> 31:57.540
This won't work.
Let's move her to the ICU!

31:57.624 --> 31:59.709
-Yes, sir.
-She's still bleeding. Is that okay?

31:59.792 --> 32:01.836
-Roll gauze, please.
-Yes, this is OR 10.

32:01.920 --> 32:04.088
We'll first put pressure
to stop the bleeding.

32:04.797 --> 32:06.507
The organs are swollen right now,

32:07.216 --> 32:09.135
so we can't spot microvascular bleeding.

32:10.136 --> 32:11.387
Let's not waste time

32:11.471 --> 32:13.473
and let the patient's condition worsen.

32:14.974 --> 32:17.602
Pack the inside, and after compression,

32:17.685 --> 32:19.520
let's open it and check
before closing her up.

32:31.950 --> 32:33.910
CURRENT TIME, SURGERY TIME

32:33.993 --> 32:34.953
LABOR ROOM

32:35.036 --> 32:37.121
It's still 4:20 p.m.!

32:37.205 --> 32:38.331
I can hold…

32:38.414 --> 32:39.540
I can hold it.

32:39.624 --> 32:41.209
Wait!

32:47.090 --> 32:47.924
The fortune teller

32:48.549 --> 32:50.009
said a January 1st birth

32:50.885 --> 32:52.470
will lead to a future as president.

32:53.054 --> 32:55.431
-Ma'am.
-Can we wait a bit?

32:56.599 --> 32:57.809
Just a few hours.

33:00.603 --> 33:03.815
I really can't give birth on the 31st!

33:03.898 --> 33:04.941
I'm sorry.

33:05.024 --> 33:07.235
The baby's the one
who chooses when to come out.

33:07.318 --> 33:08.987
We'll push when I count to three.

33:09.070 --> 33:10.822
One, two, three!

33:20.832 --> 33:22.625
The baby's out.

33:22.709 --> 33:23.960
Hi!

33:24.961 --> 33:26.838
You did so well.

33:30.591 --> 33:32.927
We just need to remove the placenta.

33:34.846 --> 33:37.515
Is my baby okay?

33:37.598 --> 33:39.183
Yes, you can hold him soon.

33:43.104 --> 33:45.648
-Yi-young, let's remove the placenta.
-Yes, ma'am.

33:52.030 --> 33:53.156
Me?

33:53.239 --> 33:54.615
I'm still…

33:55.366 --> 33:57.243
I told you everything you need to do.

34:08.796 --> 34:10.590
Gently.

34:16.095 --> 34:17.138
Don't pull…

34:20.224 --> 34:21.059
Move.

34:26.981 --> 34:29.776
I said don't pull all at once.

34:30.359 --> 34:31.861
If you try to yank it out,

34:31.944 --> 34:34.906
the cord breaks off from the placenta.

34:35.865 --> 34:36.824
I'm sorry.

34:37.492 --> 34:40.453
Mom's name is Yong Hui-seon,
and Dad's name is Jeon Tae-san, right?

34:40.995 --> 34:41.996
Yes.

34:42.080 --> 34:46.334
Time of birth is 4:28 p.m. on December 31.

34:47.460 --> 34:48.920
I'm so sorry.

34:50.588 --> 34:51.547
Mommy

34:53.049 --> 34:56.302
let you out too soon, so I'm sorry.

35:21.702 --> 35:22.537
Gosh.

35:24.080 --> 35:25.498
It really is the year's end.

35:27.750 --> 35:28.584
Doctor.

35:29.460 --> 35:30.628
Yes?

35:30.711 --> 35:32.255
I was about to call you.

35:32.338 --> 35:33.464
What is it?

35:35.883 --> 35:37.301
I think you should come see.

35:37.385 --> 35:38.219
Okay.

35:40.596 --> 35:42.431
She's a recurrent
gynecologic cancer patient,

35:42.515 --> 35:44.767
presenting with
general weakness and dyspnea.

35:45.560 --> 35:47.395
Her labs are all over the place,

35:47.478 --> 35:48.771
and her BP keeps dropping.

35:49.605 --> 35:51.190
She's currently bedridden.

35:51.274 --> 35:52.441
What's her BP?

35:53.609 --> 35:55.778
She's on vasopressors,
but BP's 60 over 40.

35:57.113 --> 35:58.990
That means her condition is really bad.

35:59.073 --> 36:02.410
I checked and she already signed a DNR.

36:02.493 --> 36:05.037
Okay. I'll take a look.

36:07.540 --> 36:08.541
What's her name?

36:09.458 --> 36:10.376
Yeom Mi-so.

36:12.670 --> 36:16.966
Age 38. After getting
her last cancer treatment here in October,

36:17.049 --> 36:18.426
she was receiving follow-up care.

36:38.821 --> 36:41.657
Did you check Ms. Yong Hui-seon's
uterine contractions?

36:41.741 --> 36:43.201
Yes, I just checked.

36:43.284 --> 36:45.077
Contractions were fine with no hematoma.

36:45.828 --> 36:46.829
That's a relief.

36:47.580 --> 36:49.707
What about that fortune thing?
Did you work it out?

36:49.790 --> 36:51.459
I managed to persuade her.

36:53.252 --> 36:54.337
I mean the fortune teller.

36:54.420 --> 36:55.379
What?

36:55.463 --> 36:57.048
I took the call instead.

36:57.131 --> 36:59.592
If he's born on January 1st,
he'll only be lucky later in life

36:59.675 --> 37:01.052
and become president at 80.

37:01.636 --> 37:03.179
If he's born on the 31st,

37:03.262 --> 37:05.473
he'll become prime minister
but the youngest on record.

37:06.057 --> 37:07.141
That's what we agreed to.

37:10.144 --> 37:11.437
You can't remove a placenta,

37:12.063 --> 37:13.689
but you deal with complaints well.

37:16.609 --> 37:18.861
Nice work. Go eat dinner.

37:18.945 --> 37:19.820
Thank you, ma'am.

37:27.870 --> 37:28.704
Okay.

37:31.999 --> 37:33.334
Yes, I understand.

37:38.089 --> 37:39.715
There's no space in the ward.

37:39.799 --> 37:42.593
Her guardian will have to come here.

37:43.219 --> 37:44.053
Okay.

37:51.185 --> 37:52.436
She likes silence

37:54.021 --> 37:55.731
and being alone though.

37:58.442 --> 38:00.152
Why today of all days?

38:00.945 --> 38:02.029
Do you know her?

38:03.489 --> 38:07.201
Yes. She was my first patient in GYN.

38:08.452 --> 38:09.787
I once ran away,

38:10.663 --> 38:12.540
but came back to see her.

38:17.545 --> 38:20.214
I'll finish writing up her chart.

38:33.394 --> 38:34.270
Ms. Yeom.

38:35.896 --> 38:37.898
Your brother is on his way.

38:39.567 --> 38:41.402
The professor will be here soon too.

38:42.028 --> 38:43.946
Things aren't looking good right now.

38:44.739 --> 38:48.409
Would you like to keep the DNR you signed?

38:52.955 --> 38:53.789
Okay.

38:55.958 --> 38:58.085
Painkillers are still being administered.

39:01.881 --> 39:03.341
Are your lips dry?

39:04.508 --> 39:06.552
Would you like me to place
a wet gauze on them?

39:12.058 --> 39:12.892
Then…

39:15.311 --> 39:16.479
Then, now…

39:19.023 --> 39:20.524
There's nothing else I can do.

39:43.130 --> 39:44.131
I'm

39:45.091 --> 39:46.550
really good at this job now.

39:47.718 --> 39:49.095
I get a lot of praise too.

39:52.681 --> 39:53.849
It's all thanks to you.

40:18.958 --> 40:20.292
RESTRICTED

40:29.343 --> 40:31.053
Sa-bi, what are you doing here?

40:31.137 --> 40:33.931
I was writing up charts
and checking on patients too.

40:34.014 --> 40:35.474
There won't be much to do for now.

40:35.558 --> 40:37.476
Go to the lounge. I'll call you.

40:37.560 --> 40:38.436
It's okay.

40:38.519 --> 40:40.521
Then, at least go eat something.

40:40.604 --> 40:43.566
I have to log surgical records anyway.
I'll keep an eye on things.

40:44.150 --> 40:45.359
It's okay though…

40:45.443 --> 40:47.111
Doctor, vitals are dropping!

40:57.663 --> 40:59.874
Professor, I think Ms. So
has active bleeding.

40:59.957 --> 41:01.167
Her pulse is at 110,

41:01.250 --> 41:03.752
and mean BP's still under 60
even on norepinephrine.

41:03.836 --> 41:05.045
We can't wait longer.

41:06.255 --> 41:07.339
Okay, sir.

41:09.175 --> 41:12.178
Anesthesiology? The patient who was
just in OR 10 needs reoperation.

41:13.220 --> 41:14.763
Yes. Let's move her.

41:14.847 --> 41:16.056
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

41:21.103 --> 41:22.855
Get that camera away from me!

41:22.938 --> 41:24.398
I think you need to come now.

41:25.566 --> 41:27.776
Doctor, just one more hour.

41:28.611 --> 41:29.987
No, now!

41:30.070 --> 41:31.572
It hurts too much!

41:32.907 --> 41:35.075
-Let's move to the delivery room.
-Wait.

41:35.159 --> 41:36.494
Can't we go a bit later?

41:36.577 --> 41:37.620
We can't.

41:37.703 --> 41:40.331
But I showed the preview
on the livestream earlier!

41:40.414 --> 41:41.916
Just one more hour.

41:41.999 --> 41:43.501
No New Year's baby would be a waste.

41:43.584 --> 41:44.752
It's not a waste at all.

41:45.503 --> 41:48.047
This is the best time to deliver.
Trust me. I know.

41:48.130 --> 41:49.131
What?

41:49.215 --> 41:51.467
The baby's ready
and so is the delivery room.

41:52.134 --> 41:54.386
Once you're ready,
everything will be perfect.

41:54.470 --> 41:56.180
-Let's move.
-Hurry!

41:56.889 --> 41:57.765
Honey.

41:57.848 --> 41:59.099
Hi!

42:09.652 --> 42:10.861
CURRENT TIME

42:10.945 --> 42:13.906
Mom's name is Moon Jin-hui,
and Dad's name is Song Ji-hwan.

42:13.989 --> 42:17.868
Time of birth is 11:02 p.m.
on December 31.

42:17.952 --> 42:18.786
Right.

42:21.664 --> 42:23.499
Unfortunately, he wasn't
a New Year's baby,

42:23.582 --> 42:25.751
but he'll always be your bundle of--

42:25.834 --> 42:26.669
Doctor.

42:28.170 --> 42:30.839
They said babies don't look pretty
right when they're born…

42:34.093 --> 42:36.053
but why is he so beautiful?

42:42.935 --> 42:44.353
He really is very cute.

42:47.022 --> 42:47.856
Yi-young.

42:48.899 --> 42:51.944
This is your last chance of the year.
Well? Want to try again?

42:56.782 --> 42:57.658
Yes.

43:02.329 --> 43:04.623
-I mean, no. I misspoke--
-Come here.

43:20.639 --> 43:22.141
Now take your left hand.

43:22.224 --> 43:25.185
I'll make sure to take out the placenta
without breaking the cord.

43:39.867 --> 43:41.285
The placenta's out.

43:42.119 --> 43:44.330
-Start the oxytocin.
-Yes, ma'am.

43:49.877 --> 43:51.045
Good.

43:58.385 --> 44:01.597
DELIVERY ROOM

44:01.680 --> 44:04.850
She must be disappointed
it wasn't a New Year's baby.

44:04.933 --> 44:05.809
No.

44:05.893 --> 44:09.021
She's happy she can greet
the new year with her baby.

44:09.104 --> 44:11.315
She and her husband
are busy filming right now.

44:12.483 --> 44:14.860
By the way, Professor,
you fulfilled your wish today.

44:15.903 --> 44:16.945
It was your wish

44:17.029 --> 44:19.782
to have a first-year wrap up
a delivery before the year's end.

44:21.116 --> 44:21.992
You're right.

44:23.619 --> 44:25.746
Great work today.

44:26.580 --> 44:27.498
See you next year.

44:31.669 --> 44:34.046
You were terrible this afternoon.
What happened?

44:36.173 --> 44:37.132
Well…

44:38.133 --> 44:40.928
It's embarrassing
to screw up all the time.

44:41.887 --> 44:43.347
And I'm the one making the mistake,

44:44.348 --> 44:47.059
but it scared me to think
the patient would suffer for it.

44:48.977 --> 44:50.729
So I looked up some videos.

44:56.402 --> 44:57.903
I didn't only look them up.

44:58.529 --> 44:59.363
I…

44:59.446 --> 45:01.615
I practiced too.

45:01.698 --> 45:03.242
In the air, like this…

45:04.243 --> 45:06.745
Why are you scared?
I'm complimenting you for doing well.

45:08.705 --> 45:09.748
You did well.

45:10.791 --> 45:12.751
You did so well

45:13.627 --> 45:15.629
it reminded me of myself
when I was a first-year.

45:17.214 --> 45:18.048
I see.

45:18.132 --> 45:19.967
Hey, that was a huge compliment.

45:22.636 --> 45:23.470
Thank you.

45:26.181 --> 45:30.394
Yi-young, can you come with me somewhere?

45:30.477 --> 45:31.395
Where?

45:31.478 --> 45:32.479
Someplace nice.

45:48.454 --> 45:49.955
You're sleeping here again?

45:55.836 --> 45:59.006
Is that all you've learned this past year?
Being able to sleep anywhere?

46:00.215 --> 46:01.091
I'm sorry.

46:01.175 --> 46:02.551
You can't sleep while on call.

46:02.634 --> 46:04.094
You have to work.

46:05.053 --> 46:07.681
I'm the one on call tonight, Professor.

46:09.892 --> 46:11.435
Then, what's he doing here?

46:12.561 --> 46:16.064
Ms. Hong Sa-ra
continues to suffer from pain.

46:16.148 --> 46:17.357
So?

46:18.984 --> 46:22.404
I was keeping her company
and chatting with her.

46:23.906 --> 46:26.742
And I was wondering about
what else I could do for her.

46:29.411 --> 46:33.081
It's Ms. Hong. She must be in pain again.

46:41.715 --> 46:43.217
It's me again.

46:44.384 --> 46:46.720
Are you feeling any discomfort?

46:46.803 --> 46:48.972
No, it's not that.

46:50.182 --> 46:52.726
It's just so strange
that I don't feel any pain.

46:53.894 --> 46:57.898
Before, even brushing against the bed
was so excruciating

46:57.981 --> 46:59.775
that I couldn't sleep at all.

47:00.359 --> 47:03.779
But I slept for four hours straight today.

47:05.364 --> 47:07.533
Did her condition improve?

47:09.243 --> 47:11.745
Her lab results haven't changed much.

47:13.997 --> 47:16.458
I came across something in a book.

47:17.417 --> 47:18.752
According to textbooks

47:18.835 --> 47:20.796
and the Cancer Center's
guidelines on pain,

47:21.380 --> 47:23.549
when pain from bone metastasis
or neuropathy

47:24.132 --> 47:26.593
can't be controlled by opioids,

47:26.677 --> 47:29.388
adding adjuvant medication
can be effective.

47:30.097 --> 47:33.016
So I looked up some related papers.

47:39.189 --> 47:42.568
Adding diazepam and dexamethasone

47:42.651 --> 47:44.361
helps reduce muscle spasms

47:44.444 --> 47:46.863
and inflammation around the tumor,

47:46.947 --> 47:50.701
and they said that would help
relieve the pain.

47:53.161 --> 47:54.788
Instead of just keeping her company,

47:55.706 --> 47:57.958
I wanted to try some other things too.

47:58.625 --> 47:59.543
So that's why…

48:00.377 --> 48:01.962
It was so good, Doctor.

48:03.630 --> 48:05.215
Maybe it's because I slept well,

48:06.091 --> 48:09.303
but when I saw myself in the mirror,
I didn't seem like a patient at all.

48:10.387 --> 48:12.472
Actually, my daughter

48:12.556 --> 48:14.558
is coming tomorrow
to see me for the new year.

48:15.517 --> 48:18.228
She'll see me smiling
for the first time in a while.

48:19.104 --> 48:20.731
Thank you, Doctor.

48:20.814 --> 48:22.065
It's no problem.

48:26.903 --> 48:29.906
Why did you suddenly do something
you weren't asked to do?

48:31.617 --> 48:32.743
I'm sorry, sir.

48:32.826 --> 48:34.786
Sa-bi was reading a book in the lounge…

48:37.664 --> 48:38.665
Only now?

48:39.291 --> 48:42.377
Geez, that took you long enough.

48:43.253 --> 48:44.129
I'm sorry, sir.

48:49.259 --> 48:50.135
Hey, Jae-il.

48:51.803 --> 48:54.931
I'll give you an Excel file
on ovarian cancer,

48:55.015 --> 48:56.141
so organize the data.

48:56.767 --> 48:58.226
Yes, sir.

48:58.310 --> 48:59.936
If the data looks good,

49:00.896 --> 49:04.316
I'll help you write the paper
and abstract with you as first author,

49:04.399 --> 49:05.609
so make sure you do it well.

49:06.568 --> 49:07.402
Yes, sir.

49:08.362 --> 49:09.279
Good night, Professor.

49:09.780 --> 49:11.323
Good night, Professor.

49:13.283 --> 49:14.117
Holy cow!

49:15.243 --> 49:17.037
That was amazing, Jae-il!

49:17.120 --> 49:18.622
What?

49:23.126 --> 49:24.961
Seriously, this is the first time

49:25.045 --> 49:27.422
that Prof. Jo's ever praised anyone.

49:28.882 --> 49:30.425
He didn't praise me.

49:30.509 --> 49:32.177
He wants to write a paper with you.

49:32.260 --> 49:33.929
If that's not praise, what is?

49:34.554 --> 49:36.431
I mean, Prof. Jo

49:36.515 --> 49:39.226
approached a first-year for a paper.

49:40.060 --> 49:42.896
I think this is the first time
in the history of Yulje.

49:45.065 --> 49:46.149
It's a good thing, right?

49:46.233 --> 49:47.359
Of course.

49:47.442 --> 49:49.778
You basically got a "Good job" sticker

49:49.861 --> 49:51.279
stamped on your forehead.

49:52.572 --> 49:53.824
But you'll get busier.

49:56.034 --> 49:58.453
Gosh, Jae-il.

49:58.537 --> 50:00.997
You've made it.

50:01.790 --> 50:03.625
It seemed like just yesterday
you were a fool.

50:04.668 --> 50:06.712
Dr. Cha, I thought I was a fool too.

50:06.795 --> 50:09.673
But after seeing the interns this year,
I was pretty okay.

50:10.465 --> 50:11.717
That's true.

50:12.467 --> 50:13.427
Who was it?

50:14.386 --> 50:16.096
I don't remember who it was.

50:17.514 --> 50:20.225
But he saw a bedridden patient
with a runny nose

50:21.017 --> 50:22.394
and said it was a brain fracture.

50:23.019 --> 50:26.481
Then he said,
"Doctor, I found an aortic dissection."

50:27.190 --> 50:29.484
And he called me like that,
sounding all determined.

50:31.236 --> 50:32.863
I think it was around March.

50:33.530 --> 50:34.740
Which intern was it?

50:34.823 --> 50:35.657
That

50:36.491 --> 50:37.367
was me.

50:38.368 --> 50:39.369
I did that.

50:46.668 --> 50:48.545
It was so funny then.

50:51.757 --> 50:53.675
Prof. Seo asked me to bring her something.

50:53.759 --> 50:54.634
I forgot.

50:55.510 --> 50:56.553
See you later.

50:56.636 --> 50:57.929
I think she already left.

51:17.699 --> 51:20.410
Weren't you saving this for a good day?

51:20.994 --> 51:22.704
Yeah. That day is today.

51:25.624 --> 51:26.708
Your paper got an award?

51:26.792 --> 51:27.751
No.

51:27.834 --> 51:29.002
A promotion…

51:29.085 --> 51:30.337
is probably not it.

51:31.755 --> 51:32.589
Is it your birthday?

51:32.672 --> 51:33.924
It's not.

51:35.133 --> 51:36.092
Then why?

51:37.052 --> 51:38.386
Didn't you hear earlier?

51:38.470 --> 51:40.388
I fulfilled my wish thanks to you.

51:41.932 --> 51:44.643
You closed a patient up last time

51:44.726 --> 51:46.853
and removed a placenta today.

51:46.937 --> 51:49.356
I knew you had good hands,

51:49.439 --> 51:51.566
but things like that only stand out now.

51:51.650 --> 51:53.693
In a few years,
we all end up similar in skill.

51:54.945 --> 51:56.613
Manual skills come with practice.

51:57.864 --> 52:00.534
But because you were worried
for the patient's well-being,

52:01.493 --> 52:05.330
you studied
and thought to research things.

52:05.956 --> 52:06.957
That was a surprise.

52:07.040 --> 52:09.668
Especially since
you'd always been trying to quit.

52:10.961 --> 52:13.964
That's more than enough reason
to open this.

52:15.340 --> 52:17.592
It wasn't that impressive.

52:20.887 --> 52:22.639
Still, I think
it would be nice to drink it.

52:22.722 --> 52:23.682
Should we open it?

52:23.765 --> 52:24.766
Here?

52:25.767 --> 52:28.645
You can't drink alcohol in a hospital.

52:28.728 --> 52:30.730
Then why did you bring me here?

52:33.358 --> 52:34.484
Take it and enjoy it later.

52:35.527 --> 52:37.153
Today's the perfect day for it.

52:37.237 --> 52:40.073
No, it's okay.
Let's drink it together next time outside.

52:40.824 --> 52:42.284
I want you to have it.

52:44.452 --> 52:45.328
Still…

52:50.375 --> 52:51.793
Then I'll gratefully accept.

52:59.801 --> 53:00.677
Hello?

53:01.845 --> 53:04.097
Already? Okay.

53:05.891 --> 53:08.018
My goodness.
They said Ms. Nam Seol-i's all full.

53:08.101 --> 53:09.060
All of a sudden?

53:09.144 --> 53:10.979
They'll move her after having her push.

53:11.062 --> 53:12.188
I'm off.

53:12.272 --> 53:14.900
Enjoy that and have fun
to your heart's content tonight.

53:25.327 --> 53:26.202
Professor!

53:28.413 --> 53:29.956
I'll take the alcohol next time.

53:30.749 --> 53:32.208
I said it's okay to go.

53:32.292 --> 53:33.376
You're not even on call.

53:33.460 --> 53:36.296
Still, I'm her doctor.
I'm curious how her baby is.

53:41.635 --> 53:42.469
Yes?

53:43.345 --> 53:44.846
I'll go in for delivery.

53:47.057 --> 53:48.266
Can you move her for us?

53:51.978 --> 53:53.855
Push if it hurts.

54:00.987 --> 54:02.656
You're almost done, ma'am.

54:02.739 --> 54:04.950
Just a little more
and you can see your baby.

54:05.867 --> 54:07.869
Yi-young. The baby's coming now.

54:09.454 --> 54:10.288
You receive it.

54:11.289 --> 54:12.123
What?

54:13.416 --> 54:14.751
Hurry, Doctor.

54:14.834 --> 54:17.087
All you have to do
is just put your hands out.

54:22.217 --> 54:23.051
Come on!

54:23.885 --> 54:24.761
Yes, ma'am.

54:32.143 --> 54:34.854
Ma'am, just one more final push!

54:39.234 --> 54:41.194
To get the anterior shoulder out,

54:41.277 --> 54:44.197
you have to lower the head a little.

54:45.448 --> 54:46.533
The shoulder's out!

54:47.158 --> 54:48.827
Support the neck with one hand

54:49.452 --> 54:51.454
and the back with the other.

54:51.538 --> 54:53.331
Go down to the bottom.

55:07.554 --> 55:09.389
The baby's out.

55:10.890 --> 55:11.725
Honey.

55:12.350 --> 55:13.226
He's out.

55:13.727 --> 55:15.061
Honey!

55:16.563 --> 55:17.397
You were great.

55:19.482 --> 55:20.567
You did so well.

55:25.488 --> 55:26.406
Hi.

55:28.116 --> 55:29.868
Great job. Move.

55:34.831 --> 55:36.666
Ma'am, congratulations.

55:36.750 --> 55:38.043
The baby's healthy.

55:39.044 --> 55:40.545
You can hold him soon.

55:40.628 --> 55:42.714
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

55:43.465 --> 55:44.924
Thank you.

55:48.011 --> 55:48.928
You did great.

55:50.513 --> 55:51.765
Ma'am, your baby.

55:51.848 --> 55:52.849
Hi, baby.

55:54.225 --> 55:55.518
It's your mom.

55:58.855 --> 56:00.648
Thank you for coming to me.

56:01.483 --> 56:02.317
Thank you.

56:13.453 --> 56:16.998
Mom's name is Nam Seol-i,
and Dad's name is Do Se-ho.

56:17.874 --> 56:22.087
Time of birth is 12:00 a.m.
on January 1, 2024.

56:22.670 --> 56:23.505
Really?

56:24.380 --> 56:25.590
Congratulations!

56:26.591 --> 56:27.592
It's a New Year's baby!

56:28.468 --> 56:30.720
-Congratulations.
-That's so cool.

56:35.683 --> 56:37.602
ANESTHESIA TIME, SURGERY TIME,
CURRENT TIME

56:53.034 --> 56:53.993
How is she?

57:02.627 --> 57:03.670
Good.

57:04.295 --> 57:05.713
We're tapering the norepinephrine,

57:05.797 --> 57:07.715
and vitals are staying stable.

57:10.260 --> 57:11.928
I think we got everything handled.

57:12.011 --> 57:13.930
Yes. I don't see any bleeding, Professor.

57:14.013 --> 57:17.475
Gosh, I was so scared
something bad might happen.

57:18.601 --> 57:19.936
All right, then…

57:20.019 --> 57:21.438
We will close her up for good now!

57:25.150 --> 57:27.318
-I need a 1-0 suture please.
-Yes, sir!

57:28.903 --> 57:30.280
And also…

57:30.363 --> 57:31.364
Everyone…

57:35.952 --> 57:37.579
It's already after midnight.

57:37.662 --> 57:38.788
Happy New Year!

57:38.872 --> 57:40.457
-Happy New Year!
-Happy New Year!

57:40.540 --> 57:41.416
Happy New Year!

57:42.459 --> 57:43.626
Happy New Year.

57:43.710 --> 57:44.961
You too, Dr. Kim.

57:47.422 --> 57:50.133
Let's not forget to tell the patient
when she wakes up,

57:51.009 --> 57:54.053
"It's been so long
we hardly recognized you."

57:56.181 --> 57:57.724
"It's been a whole year."

58:02.145 --> 58:04.856
"You've become so healthy in that time."

58:07.692 --> 58:08.526
No?

58:15.158 --> 58:16.034
Laugh, Sa-bi.

58:18.578 --> 58:19.787
Don't force it.

58:20.538 --> 58:22.165
I know it's not funny.

58:23.374 --> 58:26.085
Still, if we joke a little like this,

58:26.169 --> 58:28.046
the patient will smile

58:28.129 --> 58:29.631
and feel better.

58:30.423 --> 58:31.966
And they can recover quicker.

58:44.938 --> 58:45.772
Mi-so.

58:47.106 --> 58:48.816
Say hello to Mom for me.

58:50.860 --> 58:51.945
We'll meet again.

58:52.779 --> 58:53.738
And when we do…

58:56.115 --> 58:57.575
let's be together for a long time.

59:42.745 --> 59:44.289
January 1, 2024,

59:45.415 --> 59:46.374
time, 12:15 a.m.

59:47.333 --> 59:49.252
Ms. Yeom Mi-so has passed.

59:50.628 --> 59:51.588
Mi-so!

59:55.842 --> 59:56.759
Mi-so!

01:00:03.850 --> 01:00:04.934
Mi-so.

01:00:14.485 --> 01:00:15.320
Mi-so.

01:00:33.212 --> 01:00:34.380
Excuse me, Doctor?

01:00:37.967 --> 01:00:40.803
Was my sister in a lot of pain?

01:00:42.513 --> 01:00:43.556
She was sick for a while.

01:00:44.432 --> 01:00:46.726
Did she have a hard time
before she passed?

01:00:46.809 --> 01:00:50.521
She seemed to be in a lot of pain,
so we continuously gave her pain meds.

01:00:51.314 --> 01:00:55.193
I'm sure it wasn't too bad
when she passed.

01:01:01.491 --> 01:01:03.201
And she was here alone?

01:01:05.036 --> 01:01:06.412
She'd been alone her whole life.

01:01:08.790 --> 01:01:11.709
And it feels like I made her die alone.

01:01:13.795 --> 01:01:17.048
I stayed by her side.

01:01:20.301 --> 01:01:21.719
I held her hand

01:01:22.387 --> 01:01:23.346
and spoke to her.

01:01:25.598 --> 01:01:28.726
She had a favorite hymn,
so I turned it on for her.

01:01:29.894 --> 01:01:32.271
She looked peaceful, as if she was asleep.

01:01:33.064 --> 01:01:34.148
Thank you.

01:01:35.692 --> 01:01:36.526
Thank you so much.

01:02:00.800 --> 01:02:03.761
DEATH CERTIFICATE

01:02:07.682 --> 01:02:12.937
CAUSE OF DEATH

01:02:53.227 --> 01:02:55.354
We need help here! Please call OB-GYN!

01:02:56.230 --> 01:02:58.399
Ma'am, take deep breaths!

01:02:59.942 --> 01:03:01.778
Slowly.

01:03:02.820 --> 01:03:03.821
What happened?

01:03:03.905 --> 01:03:06.199
Her water broke at home.

01:03:06.282 --> 01:03:08.326
We just came up from the parking lot.

01:03:09.869 --> 01:03:11.621
How many weeks? Is it her first pregnancy?

01:03:11.704 --> 01:03:13.539
Well, I…

01:03:13.623 --> 01:03:16.375
It's my second, and I'm at 35 weeks.

01:03:18.085 --> 01:03:20.171
I still have so much time before I'm due.

01:03:24.175 --> 01:03:25.802
I can see the baby's head right now!

01:03:26.302 --> 01:03:28.179
We have to deliver the baby here.

01:03:28.262 --> 01:03:30.640
Please call the delivery room
and the doctor on call.

01:03:30.723 --> 01:03:31.557
Yes, Doctor.

01:03:32.308 --> 01:03:33.976
-Get a delivery kit ready.
-Yes, Doctor.

01:03:34.060 --> 01:03:35.144
OB-GYN?

01:03:35.228 --> 01:03:36.062
Yes.

01:03:37.939 --> 01:03:38.898
Sir, you can--

01:03:38.981 --> 01:03:40.191
Honey!

01:03:40.942 --> 01:03:43.402
Doctor, are my wife and baby okay?

01:03:44.237 --> 01:03:45.279
The baby will be out soon.

01:04:02.129 --> 01:04:04.465
The baby will come out
on the bed, so it won't fall.

01:04:04.549 --> 01:04:05.967
You can relax and receive it.

01:04:06.050 --> 01:04:07.009
Okay.

01:04:07.093 --> 01:04:07.927
What?

01:04:08.427 --> 01:04:09.303
Me?

01:04:13.432 --> 01:04:14.267
It's okay.

01:04:16.018 --> 01:04:18.729
Okay, let's take some deeper breaths.

01:04:18.813 --> 01:04:20.857
Okay, ma'am.

01:04:20.940 --> 01:04:23.359
Take in a deep breath and push.

01:04:24.026 --> 01:04:24.986
Push!

01:04:25.069 --> 01:04:28.155
Okay, great. You're doing so well.
Just one more time.

01:04:28.239 --> 01:04:30.408
Take a big breath.

01:04:30.992 --> 01:04:32.159
That's great.

01:04:32.243 --> 01:04:35.204
Okay, let's push. Push!

01:04:38.583 --> 01:04:40.751
Great, the baby's coming.

01:04:41.419 --> 01:04:43.045
Okay, this is the last part.

01:04:45.840 --> 01:04:46.716
Okay.

01:04:47.466 --> 01:04:48.509
Okay, ma'am.

01:04:48.593 --> 01:04:51.679
Take a deep breath one last time and push.

01:04:51.762 --> 01:04:54.473
Okay, take a deep breath and push.

01:04:54.557 --> 01:04:56.392
Okay. One last time, push!

01:04:59.437 --> 01:05:01.772
Ma'am. Push longer.

01:05:01.856 --> 01:05:03.983
Take in a breath and one more time.

01:05:04.066 --> 01:05:05.067
Push!

01:05:05.568 --> 01:05:08.905
One, two, three, push!

01:05:24.587 --> 01:05:27.506
January 1st.
Time, 12:24 a.m. It's a baby boy.

01:05:30.051 --> 01:05:31.761
You did great, ma'am.

01:05:34.055 --> 01:05:35.139
The baby's crying well.

01:05:56.994 --> 01:05:58.204
It's okay.

01:05:58.287 --> 01:05:59.121
What happened?

01:06:02.541 --> 01:06:04.919
A multigravida came
after her water broke at home.

01:06:05.002 --> 01:06:07.088
The baby was appearing
when she was admitted.

01:06:08.339 --> 01:06:09.215
It looks good.

01:06:09.715 --> 01:06:11.217
We'll remove the placenta upstairs.

01:06:12.134 --> 01:06:12.969
Gosh.

01:06:14.887 --> 01:06:16.055
You did well by yourself.

01:06:26.565 --> 01:06:27.692
Where did he go?

01:06:37.159 --> 01:06:38.327
Professor, the baby is fine.

01:06:38.995 --> 01:06:39.870
Okay.

01:07:23.622 --> 01:07:24.832
Are you okay?

01:07:30.171 --> 01:07:31.839
Ma'am, are you awake?

01:07:31.922 --> 01:07:32.840
Are you okay?

01:07:33.716 --> 01:07:34.592
Yes.

01:07:36.677 --> 01:07:37.678
And you, Sa-bi?

01:07:38.554 --> 01:07:39.638
Are you okay?

01:07:39.722 --> 01:07:40.765
Sir?

01:07:41.891 --> 01:07:42.725
Yes.

01:07:45.269 --> 01:07:46.437
I've been monitoring her.

01:07:46.520 --> 01:07:49.148
Urine output's good
and her vitals are stable.

01:07:49.732 --> 01:07:51.859
I've tapered off the norepinephrine.

01:07:53.110 --> 01:07:55.404
I checked your blood work.
It all looks good.

01:07:56.030 --> 01:07:57.782
First, get some rest,

01:07:57.865 --> 01:08:00.159
and you can focus on recovery.

01:08:04.705 --> 01:08:05.748
And…

01:08:09.919 --> 01:08:13.631
The bleeding didn't stop initially,
so there were a few things that happened.

01:08:13.714 --> 01:08:17.718
But I will explain everything
in detail later.

01:08:20.221 --> 01:08:21.388
There's more though.

01:08:27.061 --> 01:08:29.021
As soon as your bed is ready,

01:08:29.105 --> 01:08:30.397
you'll go into the ward.

01:08:30.481 --> 01:08:32.274
I'll explain it to you then.

01:08:34.944 --> 01:08:36.654
And one more thing.

01:08:44.245 --> 01:08:45.412
It's been so long,

01:08:46.455 --> 01:08:47.832
I almost didn't recognize you.

01:08:49.250 --> 01:08:50.126
It's been a year.

01:08:55.214 --> 01:08:56.048
Gosh.

01:08:56.966 --> 01:08:59.718
You've become so healthy in that time.

01:09:05.015 --> 01:09:07.935
So it's January 1st.

01:09:09.854 --> 01:09:12.481
The professor said
you'll recover faster if you smile.

01:09:13.607 --> 01:09:14.775
Please get better soon.

01:09:16.652 --> 01:09:19.113
Thank you for working the entire year

01:09:20.072 --> 01:09:21.615
on my surgery.

01:09:23.409 --> 01:09:25.369
Happy New Year.

01:09:29.707 --> 01:09:31.000
Happy New Year.

01:09:31.709 --> 01:09:32.877
Happy New Year.

01:09:48.017 --> 01:09:50.186
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

01:09:53.022 --> 01:09:55.107
OB-GYN
1ST-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE

01:10:02.489 --> 01:10:03.324
Hey.

01:10:05.367 --> 01:10:06.368
Are you sleeping?

01:10:09.622 --> 01:10:10.623
Get up.

01:10:13.500 --> 01:10:14.877
Did you just get back?

01:10:14.960 --> 01:10:16.962
You didn't go home?

01:10:18.130 --> 01:10:19.715
We couldn't.

01:10:20.424 --> 01:10:21.592
I'm so hungry.

01:10:22.635 --> 01:10:23.469
Me too.

01:10:24.929 --> 01:10:26.263
I'm hungry too.

01:10:34.063 --> 01:10:34.980
It's good.

01:10:35.064 --> 01:10:36.649
What do you mean? They're all bloated.

01:10:36.732 --> 01:10:39.109
The bigger rice cakes will mean
a more bountiful year.

01:10:39.193 --> 01:10:40.361
Isn't that for Chuseok?

01:10:40.444 --> 01:10:41.987
It's good for any time of the year.

01:10:42.071 --> 01:10:44.198
Bountiful pockets and hearts.

01:10:44.281 --> 01:10:46.200
And work… is probably not.

01:10:46.283 --> 01:10:49.453
I just happened to read
my fortune for this year.

01:10:50.621 --> 01:10:52.665
I'm all out of luck in all areas

01:10:52.748 --> 01:10:53.999
except for work.

01:10:54.083 --> 01:10:55.709
We're second-years now.

01:10:55.793 --> 01:10:57.253
Dr. Eun-mi said

01:10:57.336 --> 01:10:59.588
to think of it as being twice
as busy as we are now.

01:10:59.672 --> 01:11:01.257
Gosh, I can't do a second year.

01:11:02.466 --> 01:11:04.343
No, I won't. How can I?

01:11:04.927 --> 01:11:06.095
I'm so tired of that.

01:11:06.178 --> 01:11:07.805
People like her stay the longest.

01:11:07.888 --> 01:11:09.640
It's her habit of speaking now.

01:11:11.517 --> 01:11:13.727
I was going to tell you guys.

01:11:16.605 --> 01:11:18.065
I'm not doing my second year.

01:11:19.358 --> 01:11:21.402
I'm going to quit at the end of February.

01:11:21.485 --> 01:11:23.028
Hey, do we have kimchi in the fridge?

01:11:23.112 --> 01:11:24.321
No, it's all gone.

01:11:25.239 --> 01:11:26.657
Eat the whole rice cake. It's good.

01:11:28.242 --> 01:11:29.868
I'm serious.

01:11:32.329 --> 01:11:34.248
I wasn't going to tell you this, but…

01:11:37.876 --> 01:11:40.045
I won the lottery.

01:11:47.303 --> 01:11:48.637
So I don't need to work.

01:11:51.932 --> 01:11:52.808
Liar.

01:11:52.891 --> 01:11:53.809
Come on.

01:11:53.892 --> 01:11:54.810
No way.

01:11:59.356 --> 01:12:00.691
Goodness.

01:12:01.859 --> 01:12:05.112
I don't know
if you've ever seen such a thing before.

01:12:09.283 --> 01:12:10.242
Ta-da!

01:12:12.202 --> 01:12:13.912
This will cover all of my debt.

01:12:13.996 --> 01:12:16.332
So I can quit being a resident.

01:12:17.624 --> 01:12:19.710
Well, I'm going to rest

01:12:19.793 --> 01:12:22.129
and look for other work.

01:12:22.671 --> 01:12:23.589
Oh, dear.

01:12:27.426 --> 01:12:28.344
Goodness.

01:12:35.976 --> 01:12:36.894
Wait, what the…

01:12:39.521 --> 01:12:41.774
THE CLAIM PERIOD HAS EXPIRED

01:12:46.570 --> 01:12:47.446
No.

01:12:48.405 --> 01:12:50.449
No!

01:13:01.001 --> 01:13:02.336
What are you taking home?

01:13:02.419 --> 01:13:04.046
-A taxi.
-The bus.

01:13:04.129 --> 01:13:05.839
-Me too.
-The bus for me too.

01:13:07.299 --> 01:13:08.217
Oh, right!

01:13:09.093 --> 01:13:10.594
Damn it, nothing's going my way.

01:13:11.220 --> 01:13:12.221
I'll see you later.

01:13:15.099 --> 01:13:15.933
Where is she going?

01:13:16.600 --> 01:13:17.976
On a date, of course.

01:13:21.355 --> 01:13:22.606
Oh, my gosh!

01:13:22.689 --> 01:13:24.149
What is it? Are you in pain?

01:13:24.233 --> 01:13:25.401
Yeah, my stomach hurts.

01:13:25.484 --> 01:13:26.443
Because I'm so jealous.

01:13:28.695 --> 01:13:30.739
Right. Bye.

01:13:31.740 --> 01:13:32.616
See you tomorrow.

01:13:33.117 --> 01:13:34.827
-Happy New Year.
-You too.

01:13:44.044 --> 01:13:44.878
Let's go.

01:13:50.634 --> 01:13:51.885
Wow, it's snowing.

01:13:52.678 --> 01:13:54.346
On the first day of the year too.

01:13:56.849 --> 01:14:00.185
Hey, I'm going to write a paper
on ovarian cancer with Prof. Jo.

01:14:01.103 --> 01:14:02.104
And that means,

01:14:02.688 --> 01:14:05.983
I'm his first-ever first-year mentee.

01:14:06.066 --> 01:14:09.194
Ovarian cancer? Then look up
Prof. Ryu's paper from last year.

01:14:09.278 --> 01:14:12.156
It's a good reference for how they set up
patient and control groups.

01:14:13.574 --> 01:14:14.450
Thanks.

01:14:15.492 --> 01:14:17.494
How do you remember
every paper you read though?

01:14:17.578 --> 01:14:19.913
I organize them
by publication year and importance.

01:14:20.622 --> 01:14:22.374
And I write down what I'm curious about

01:14:22.458 --> 01:14:24.626
and resolve them
before moving on to the next chapter.

01:14:24.710 --> 01:14:25.836
That's my strict rule.

01:14:28.547 --> 01:14:30.924
When you talk about your rules,
you're the cutest…

01:14:41.894 --> 01:14:44.646
Hey, you already know,

01:14:45.355 --> 01:14:48.275
but I'm the type who needs
to resolve things I'm curious about.

01:14:50.819 --> 01:14:52.404
Do you like me?

01:14:53.405 --> 01:14:55.824
I didn't want to get you wrong,
so I thought about it.

01:14:55.908 --> 01:14:58.160
First was karaoke.
Second was the outpatient churros.

01:14:58.243 --> 01:15:01.038
And third was
when you were in the wheelchair.

01:15:01.121 --> 01:15:03.749
If you weren't in pain,
but pretended to be, that means--

01:15:03.832 --> 01:15:04.666
Hey.

01:15:05.667 --> 01:15:07.878
What's with the step-by-step questioning?

01:15:08.504 --> 01:15:10.797
And why are you so curious?

01:15:11.548 --> 01:15:12.382
Of course…

01:15:15.177 --> 01:15:16.512
I like you.

01:15:19.848 --> 01:15:21.183
Everything you said was right.

01:15:22.518 --> 01:15:23.810
You made the right conclusion.

01:15:25.437 --> 01:15:26.313
I…

01:15:28.774 --> 01:15:29.775
like you.

01:15:35.113 --> 01:15:35.989
What about you?

01:15:38.575 --> 01:15:40.994
-If you like me too…
-No!

01:15:43.830 --> 01:15:45.874
I think about you too,

01:15:45.958 --> 01:15:48.085
and it is true that I miss you at times.

01:15:51.964 --> 01:15:53.674
But I don't think I'm ready to date yet.

01:15:54.716 --> 01:15:57.594
They say you need at least a year
to get to know someone first.

01:15:57.678 --> 01:15:59.555
It's a strict rule of mine too.

01:15:59.638 --> 01:16:01.390
Hey, I didn't ask you to marry me.

01:16:01.473 --> 01:16:02.933
Who needs strict rules for dating?

01:16:03.016 --> 01:16:03.850
I do.

01:16:04.518 --> 01:16:06.645
We met last March,

01:16:07.229 --> 01:16:09.731
so I still need to get to know you more.

01:16:10.691 --> 01:16:12.109
I don't need to see anymore, okay?

01:16:12.192 --> 01:16:13.902
You know me enough already, Sa-bi.

01:16:13.986 --> 01:16:15.654
I really like you.

01:16:15.737 --> 01:16:17.239
Hey, stop saying that.

01:16:17.322 --> 01:16:19.408
Kim Sa-bi, I like you a lot.

01:16:20.075 --> 01:16:21.159
I said stop!

01:16:21.243 --> 01:16:22.327
Sa-bi, I like you!

01:16:23.287 --> 01:16:30.252
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

01:16:37.843 --> 01:16:38.844
Are you going home?

01:16:39.761 --> 01:16:40.596
Yes.

01:16:50.063 --> 01:16:50.939
Are you okay?

01:16:51.690 --> 01:16:52.566
What?

01:16:57.029 --> 01:16:57.863
Yes.

01:17:02.075 --> 01:17:03.702
Thanks for today.

01:17:05.662 --> 01:17:06.496
Sure.

01:17:18.634 --> 01:17:19.468
Doctor.

01:17:21.470 --> 01:17:23.055
I chose which department to go to.

01:17:26.308 --> 01:17:27.726
Don't you want to know which one?

01:17:30.562 --> 01:17:31.396
OB-GYN.

01:17:32.481 --> 01:17:33.607
I'm going to join OB-GYN.

01:17:34.524 --> 01:17:35.359
Really?

01:17:36.985 --> 01:17:38.236
You're serious, right?

01:17:38.320 --> 01:17:39.780
No takebacks.

01:17:39.863 --> 01:17:41.281
You've promised to come. Okay?

01:17:42.449 --> 01:17:43.325
Okay.

01:17:43.408 --> 01:17:44.910
You made the right choice.

01:17:44.993 --> 01:17:46.745
You won't regret it.

01:17:46.828 --> 01:17:48.914
I'll be really good to you.

01:17:50.123 --> 01:17:50.957
Okay.

01:17:56.755 --> 01:17:58.173
I look forward to working with you.

01:18:02.094 --> 01:18:03.261
Me too.

01:18:50.892 --> 01:18:51.727
I'm so sorry.

01:18:52.310 --> 01:18:53.937
I had a really hectic day today.

01:18:58.108 --> 01:18:58.984
What?

01:19:01.403 --> 01:19:03.196
How did you know I was here?

01:19:03.280 --> 01:19:05.365
You didn't pick up
and weren't at the lounge.

01:19:05.449 --> 01:19:06.616
I figured I'd come by here.

01:19:08.994 --> 01:19:10.370
It's still January 1st.

01:19:10.454 --> 01:19:12.456
It's 11:40 p.m. We have 20 minutes left.

01:19:17.252 --> 01:19:18.253
I mean,

01:19:18.837 --> 01:19:21.673
babies were coming out
and mothers were in labor left and right.

01:19:22.299 --> 01:19:25.802
And I had all my debt repaid,
but all my money disappeared.

01:19:25.886 --> 01:19:27.179
Nothing went right today…

01:19:31.850 --> 01:19:33.935
I didn't want to give them to you here.

01:19:35.729 --> 01:19:36.563
I failed again

01:19:37.230 --> 01:19:38.315
to surprise you.

01:19:41.526 --> 01:19:42.736
What is that?

01:19:45.989 --> 01:19:46.907
Ah, this.

01:19:46.990 --> 01:19:50.994
I was proud of you
for bravely completing your first year

01:19:52.454 --> 01:19:55.582
and wanted to
wish you luck on your second.

01:19:58.376 --> 01:20:01.046
Yes. Thank you, Dr. Ku.

01:20:09.554 --> 01:20:11.807
But is it okay over there?

01:20:12.390 --> 01:20:13.266
Over where?

01:20:13.892 --> 01:20:16.186
Well, on your seat…

01:20:27.113 --> 01:20:29.574
I really didn't mean
to give that to you this way either.

01:20:35.914 --> 01:20:36.790
Here.

01:20:48.885 --> 01:20:51.680
Why are you giving me this?

01:20:57.185 --> 01:20:58.186
Because I like you.

01:21:59.205 --> 01:22:01.499
Now, today's guest of honor,

01:22:01.583 --> 01:22:04.878
Professor Im Dong-ju from OB-GYN
will give his retirement speech.

01:22:14.471 --> 01:22:21.436
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR RETIREMENT
PROFESSOR IM DONG-JU, OB-GYN

01:22:24.564 --> 01:22:26.566
I've been an OB-GYN doctor

01:22:27.525 --> 01:22:29.903
for already 40 years now.

01:22:30.904 --> 01:22:33.823
Facing the timeless truth
of life and death every day,

01:22:34.407 --> 01:22:38.036
I've said countless farewells.

01:22:38.828 --> 01:22:40.580
But my farewell to you today

01:22:41.164 --> 01:22:43.458
will be the hardest to bear.

01:22:44.834 --> 01:22:48.004
I might be a bit late in admitting this,

01:22:48.546 --> 01:22:51.800
but to be honest,
I always came in last place.

01:22:55.095 --> 01:22:58.723
I was never a good student
and suffered from an inferiority complex.

01:22:59.307 --> 01:23:01.685
My nose was always buried in books,

01:23:02.644 --> 01:23:04.854
so I was dead last
in emotional growth too.

01:23:07.482 --> 01:23:11.569
Despite all that, I can retire today
after enjoying a full career

01:23:12.153 --> 01:23:15.156
thanks to all the amazing people

01:23:15.740 --> 01:23:17.409
I met here at Yulje.

01:23:19.411 --> 01:23:21.663
In ways seen or unseen,

01:23:22.205 --> 01:23:24.582
through every moment of despair and joy,

01:23:25.333 --> 01:23:27.627
to those who gave me trust and faith…

01:23:27.711 --> 01:23:31.548
I wanted to select someone who can provide

01:23:31.631 --> 01:23:33.675
trust and faith in every moment.

01:23:34.926 --> 01:23:36.219
Instead of sitting at desks,

01:23:36.302 --> 01:23:39.848
looking at pieces of papers like us,

01:23:39.931 --> 01:23:43.893
our nurses and residents spend more time
working together in the field,

01:23:43.977 --> 01:23:46.062
and I thought they'd know better than us.

01:23:46.646 --> 01:23:48.273
So I asked for their advice,

01:23:49.274 --> 01:23:51.192
and I think it was a great help.

01:23:51.860 --> 01:23:53.486
I'd like to appoint as professor

01:23:54.070 --> 01:23:56.781
someone who focuses on taking an honest

01:23:57.615 --> 01:24:00.160
and upright approach to the process

01:24:00.243 --> 01:24:01.995
over the end result.

01:24:02.871 --> 01:24:05.457
Therefore, our new OB professor will be…

01:24:10.628 --> 01:24:12.630
this person.

01:24:15.675 --> 01:24:16.801
Hello, Professor.

01:24:18.595 --> 01:24:21.056
Thank you for letting me know so quickly.

01:24:22.348 --> 01:24:24.184
It's all right. Don't worry.

01:24:26.227 --> 01:24:27.395
Yes, Professor.

01:24:29.355 --> 01:24:30.398
Okay, bye.

01:24:44.829 --> 01:24:48.833
Also, there were so many patients

01:24:48.917 --> 01:24:50.543
who became great teachers

01:24:51.044 --> 01:24:53.171
in my journey of personal growth.

01:24:53.963 --> 01:24:55.173
And among them,

01:24:55.256 --> 01:24:59.344
it's thanks to those who taught me
how to fail with grace

01:24:59.928 --> 01:25:02.722
and to let go with courage

01:25:04.015 --> 01:25:08.186
that I was able to become a better person.

01:25:09.312 --> 01:25:11.272
The blood test results came back,

01:25:12.273 --> 01:25:14.359
and it's under 0.2.

01:25:15.652 --> 01:25:16.653
You're not

01:25:17.445 --> 01:25:18.363
pregnant.

01:25:19.823 --> 01:25:21.825
Professor, by any chance…

01:25:21.908 --> 01:25:25.203
What if we tried a second blood test?

01:25:25.787 --> 01:25:27.705
It would be pointless.

01:25:28.665 --> 01:25:29.833
I see.

01:25:29.916 --> 01:25:33.169
You should rest for a few months,

01:25:33.253 --> 01:25:34.587
get your strength up,

01:25:35.171 --> 01:25:36.673
and refresh your minds.

01:25:36.756 --> 01:25:38.675
Then we can start again
with egg retrieval.

01:25:38.758 --> 01:25:40.677
There's a lot of patients who succeeded

01:25:40.760 --> 01:25:42.887
after more than ten attempts.

01:25:44.013 --> 01:25:45.056
Right.

01:25:46.099 --> 01:25:48.351
They must be amazing people.

01:25:49.602 --> 01:25:50.812
But I

01:25:52.438 --> 01:25:54.482
don't think I'm one of them.

01:26:03.616 --> 01:26:04.450
I…

01:26:06.619 --> 01:26:07.829
would like to stop.

01:26:15.420 --> 01:26:17.797
We'd like to stop here.

01:26:19.382 --> 01:26:22.594
If we had a baby, it would be beautiful,
and we'd be so happy.

01:26:23.845 --> 01:26:25.555
That's why mothers say,

01:26:25.638 --> 01:26:29.809
"Gosh, I guess I was born
to meet my baby."

01:26:32.520 --> 01:26:34.898
People say a baby completes a family

01:26:35.481 --> 01:26:38.359
and wonder how can you live
without that happiness.

01:26:41.738 --> 01:26:43.489
But I'll give that life a shot.

01:26:44.324 --> 01:26:47.952
My family may be incomplete to some,
but I am happy with it.

01:26:50.246 --> 01:26:51.706
The joy a baby brings

01:26:52.916 --> 01:26:55.627
is something I'll try to find
elsewhere on my own.

01:26:57.128 --> 01:27:00.131
I won't resent myself anymore.

01:27:02.217 --> 01:27:03.676
I'll love myself

01:27:04.636 --> 01:27:06.221
and try to live a happy life.

01:27:08.681 --> 01:27:10.350
Thank you for all your help, Professor.

01:27:10.433 --> 01:27:12.852
All right. I understand.

01:27:22.779 --> 01:27:24.072
Thanks to all of them,

01:27:24.697 --> 01:27:28.159
I leave this place with no regrets.

01:27:31.037 --> 01:27:33.414
Thank you for everything.

01:27:34.916 --> 01:27:35.792
Once again,

01:27:37.210 --> 01:27:38.211
thank you.

01:27:51.557 --> 01:27:53.851
Thank you, thank you.

01:28:14.163 --> 01:28:16.165
-I've been seeing you a lot these days.
-I know.

01:28:16.958 --> 01:28:18.501
Funerals and retirement ceremonies…

01:28:18.584 --> 01:28:19.460
A lot's going on.

01:28:20.670 --> 01:28:22.588
Time sure does fly though.

01:28:23.506 --> 01:28:25.717
I can't believe our professor's retiring.

01:28:26.217 --> 01:28:27.093
I know.

01:28:27.719 --> 01:28:30.471
It feels like just yesterday
we took his classes in med school.

01:28:30.555 --> 01:28:31.597
Right?

01:28:31.681 --> 01:28:34.559
Back then, when we prepared
our simulation training presentations,

01:28:34.642 --> 01:28:36.561
we'd act as the patients.

01:28:37.687 --> 01:28:41.149
Back then, Ik-jun lost his voice
while simulating labor.

01:28:42.817 --> 01:28:43.860
A legendary performance.

01:28:47.030 --> 01:28:47.989
Hello.

01:28:48.072 --> 01:28:49.073
-Hello.
-Hello.

01:28:49.157 --> 01:28:50.199
-Hello.
-Hi.

01:28:50.700 --> 01:28:52.368
Our first-year residents.

01:28:52.994 --> 01:28:55.788
This is Professor Yang Seok-hyeong
from the main branch.

01:28:56.497 --> 01:28:57.665
-Hello.
-Hello.

01:29:02.920 --> 01:29:04.714
Go get some breakfast

01:29:04.797 --> 01:29:06.674
and make sure to be prepped for rounds.

01:29:06.758 --> 01:29:07.759
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes, ma'am.

01:29:09.552 --> 01:29:12.138
-Does she dislike Jae-il?
-No, she didn't say that.

01:29:12.221 --> 01:29:14.307
Hey. Gosh, I'm so jealous!

01:29:15.433 --> 01:29:16.267
Geez.

01:29:16.351 --> 01:29:17.852
So they were first-years.

01:29:17.935 --> 01:29:19.562
Yeah, aren't they cute?

01:29:20.313 --> 01:29:21.272
They're good too.

01:29:21.981 --> 01:29:23.149
It seemed like it.

01:29:23.232 --> 01:29:25.151
Good judgment and fast hands.

01:29:25.777 --> 01:29:26.694
And strong nerves.

01:29:27.320 --> 01:29:29.322
Yeah. How did you know?

01:29:31.324 --> 01:29:33.076
I can just tell by looking at them.

01:29:34.452 --> 01:29:35.787
Are you a psychic?

01:29:36.371 --> 01:29:38.664
I mean, they're your students,
so it's no surprise.

01:29:40.041 --> 01:29:42.001
You're really good at being a teacher.

01:29:42.085 --> 01:29:44.295
We wouldn't have graduated
if we didn't study with you.

01:29:45.671 --> 01:29:47.882
That was centuries ago.

01:29:48.466 --> 01:29:52.053
But with teaching,
I think I'm pretty good at it.

01:29:52.136 --> 01:29:53.096
I agree.

01:29:53.930 --> 01:29:55.014
I agree too.

01:29:56.766 --> 01:30:00.603
So I'd like to
leave it in your hands this time as well.

01:30:25.294 --> 01:30:27.839
So, we're here to say hello.

01:30:31.384 --> 01:30:32.677
It's so good to see you!

01:30:33.469 --> 01:30:35.054
We've met often at conferences, right?

01:30:35.138 --> 01:30:37.974
Yes, Professor.
It's so nice to see you again.

01:30:38.057 --> 01:30:38.891
Me too.

01:30:39.600 --> 01:30:44.814
But I can't trust you 100 percent yet.

01:30:44.897 --> 01:30:46.566
What? Why not?

01:30:46.649 --> 01:30:50.027
No matter who I ask about you,
there's only praise.

01:30:50.111 --> 01:30:51.779
Is that even possible?

01:30:52.697 --> 01:30:53.531
Well,

01:30:54.490 --> 01:30:56.742
that's because I always
take people out to eat.

01:30:56.826 --> 01:30:58.786
Someone said that too.

01:30:58.870 --> 01:31:00.329
They said you're way too humble.

01:31:03.499 --> 01:31:04.709
Doctor.

01:31:04.792 --> 01:31:06.169
I mean, Professor.

01:31:06.836 --> 01:31:08.212
It's been so long.

01:31:09.046 --> 01:31:10.798
Congratulations on becoming professor.

01:31:12.091 --> 01:31:13.593
Why are you being so awkward?

01:31:13.676 --> 01:31:15.052
Just be yourself, Do-won.

01:31:15.136 --> 01:31:17.180
How can I? You're a professor now.

01:31:17.263 --> 01:31:19.015
I need to get in your good graces.

01:31:21.350 --> 01:31:23.686
I just got here,
and I've met a great fellow.

01:31:23.769 --> 01:31:25.646
I am pretty lucky, aren't I?

01:31:26.772 --> 01:31:29.150
I should be the one
who's honored to meet you.

01:31:30.401 --> 01:31:32.320
And this is Dr. Myeong Eun-won.

01:31:32.945 --> 01:31:35.072
Right. You were
at the main branch together.

01:31:36.324 --> 01:31:37.450
Yes.

01:31:38.451 --> 01:31:40.244
How have you been, Doctor?

01:31:41.329 --> 01:31:43.372
Moving forward,
I'd really appreciate your help.

01:31:44.165 --> 01:31:45.041
Of course.

01:31:47.877 --> 01:31:50.588
I'm glad to be working with you as well…

01:31:52.131 --> 01:31:53.049
Professor.

01:31:53.925 --> 01:31:56.135
Yes. Thank you.

01:32:02.725 --> 01:32:04.143
Congrats, Professor Chu-chu.

01:32:04.810 --> 01:32:06.812
I asked for something prettier than you,

01:32:06.896 --> 01:32:08.856
but those flowers don't exist.

01:32:17.657 --> 01:32:19.617
You weren't alone.

01:32:28.834 --> 01:32:30.419
He's my husband.

01:32:30.503 --> 01:32:32.380
He must've thought no one else was here.

01:32:33.047 --> 01:32:36.008
He usually does cute things like that.

01:32:39.262 --> 01:32:41.764
Thank you for the welcome.

01:32:41.847 --> 01:32:43.766
I promise to give it my best.

01:32:43.849 --> 01:32:44.809
Let's give her a hand!

01:32:45.935 --> 01:32:47.645
Welcome!

01:32:47.728 --> 01:32:49.063
Welcome.

01:32:58.823 --> 01:33:00.283
-Bye!
-Bye!

01:33:02.243 --> 01:33:04.412
I honestly didn't think she'd last a year.

01:33:04.495 --> 01:33:05.371
Me neither.

01:33:05.454 --> 01:33:06.539
Hold on.

01:33:07.248 --> 01:33:09.333
Did she develop an interest in the work

01:33:10.126 --> 01:33:12.253
or a sense of duty?

01:33:14.046 --> 01:33:15.339
That's probably not it.

01:33:16.048 --> 01:33:16.924
Right?

01:33:17.008 --> 01:33:18.718
She has 16 million left to pay off.

01:33:19.385 --> 01:33:21.554
Let's hope she never pays it off.

01:33:23.514 --> 01:33:25.433
We should raise her rent this year.

01:33:29.729 --> 01:33:30.896
But why…

01:33:32.106 --> 01:33:33.774
They're holding hands.

01:33:36.736 --> 01:33:37.611
Holding hands?

01:33:42.533 --> 01:33:44.160
-They made up!
-That must be it!

01:33:44.744 --> 01:33:45.995
They must've made up!

01:33:46.912 --> 01:33:48.372
Gosh.

01:33:48.456 --> 01:33:52.001
They used to ignore each other
like they were sworn enemies.

01:33:52.752 --> 01:33:54.337
-What a relief.
-Right?

01:33:54.420 --> 01:33:55.838
Gosh.

01:34:03.596 --> 01:34:05.514
RESIDENT LOUNGE

01:34:15.358 --> 01:34:16.192
See you later.

01:34:42.051 --> 01:34:44.011
JOIN OUR OB-GYN TEAM
RECRUITING NEW RESIDENTS

01:34:48.974 --> 01:34:50.476
1ST-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE
OB-GYN

01:35:26.095 --> 01:35:33.060
OB-GYN
2ND-YEAR RESIDENT LOUNGE

01:35:40.067 --> 01:35:41.235
Hey, what took you so long?

01:35:41.318 --> 01:35:42.153
Here.

01:35:42.736 --> 01:35:44.071
I bought coffee. Iced, right?

01:35:44.155 --> 01:35:45.030
Yeah.

01:35:45.114 --> 01:35:47.950
Hey, your Williams book's new.
Can I give it to the first-year?

01:35:48.033 --> 01:35:49.493
No, I need it.

01:35:50.077 --> 01:35:51.245
Hey.

01:35:51.328 --> 01:35:53.414
Is that a new top? It looks new.

01:35:53.497 --> 01:35:55.749
-I've had it for a while.
-It's nice.

01:35:55.833 --> 01:35:57.334
Did anyone see a pen here?

01:35:57.418 --> 01:35:58.836
-Here.
-A blue one!

01:35:59.545 --> 01:36:00.379
Here.

01:36:01.172 --> 01:36:02.756
Hey, how's tteokbokki for lunch today?

01:36:02.840 --> 01:36:03.716
Okay!

01:36:03.799 --> 01:36:05.092
Make it spicy. With rice balls.

01:36:05.176 --> 01:36:06.260
Of course.

01:36:06.760 --> 01:36:08.471
Yi-young. You're in, right?

01:36:08.554 --> 01:36:10.556
You guys haven't changed at all.

01:36:13.976 --> 01:36:15.478
You're the same as when we first met.

01:36:18.647 --> 01:36:19.690
It's nice.

01:36:20.941 --> 01:36:22.151
What are you talking about?

01:36:22.234 --> 01:36:23.152
Come on.

01:36:23.903 --> 01:36:24.737
See you later.

01:36:25.321 --> 01:36:26.697
I think it's nice too.

01:36:38.792 --> 01:36:40.920
This is second-year resident, Oh Yi-young.

01:37:23.754 --> 01:37:27.258
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUEST, KANG SHIN-IL,
OUR PROFESSOR IM DONG-JU

01:37:27.758 --> 01:37:30.094
THANKS TO OUR SPECIAL GUESTS,
KIM DAE-MYEUNG &amp; AHN EUN-JIN,

01:37:30.177 --> 01:37:31.887
OUR ETERNAL YANG SEOK-HYEONG &amp; CHU MIN-HA

01:37:32.429 --> 01:37:35.683
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:37:40.104 --> 01:37:40.938
To…

01:37:41.981 --> 01:37:42.982
-What's that?
-…tally!

01:37:43.649 --> 01:37:44.692
Mind.

01:37:44.775 --> 01:37:45.693
Blowing.

01:37:45.776 --> 01:37:46.652
Bye!

01:39:17.951 --> 01:39:19.953
Subtitle translation by: Jamie Jin
